window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["26"]={"https://theconversation.com/minecraft-techno-raves-and-brainrot-are-modern-election-strategies-but-do-they-win-any-votes-296049":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"c3b49776728b9c700bfa3ca94f235c55f35d01c42e620abfcd082f2004e8c342","read":"https://theconversation.com/minecraft-techno-raves-and-brainrot-are-modern-election-strategies-but-do-they-win-any-votes-296049","bytes":179450,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Minecraft, techno raves and brainrot are modern election strategies, but do they win any votes?","by":[{"n":"Susan Grantham","r":"Senior Lecturer in Communication, Griffith University"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T18:23:51Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["What do Minecraft, brainrot and techno raves have in common? They have all been co-opted as political campaign strategies."]},{"k":"p","s":["With Victoria heading to the polls later this month, Victorian Labor has ventured into Minecraft, the video game where people build worlds out of blocks."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a reward for reaching 35,000 followers on Minecraft, Labor hosted a virtual party on TikTok featuring a Pauline Hanson diss track in phonk (a sub-genre of hip hop) style. Premier Ben Carroll even appeared to DJ on the TikTok live stream, though his button-pressing didn’t always seem to match the music."]},{"k":"p","s":["The event peaked at around 600 participants, with average attendance closer to 200. Which raises an obvious question: who exactly was this for?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Were young voters suddenly inspired to investigate Labor’s policies? Was it aimed at younger children whose parents might be potential Labor voters? Or was the real audience everyone watching clips of a politician pretending to DJ in a block-shaped universe?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Welcome to modern political campaigning, where winning the algorithm can sometimes seem more important than winning an argument."]},{"k":"h","s":["From Italian brainrot to political brainrot"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not the first time we have seen a trend-driven campaign. Labor famously used TikTok in its winning ",["2022 federal election campaign","https://doi.org/10.1080/22041451.2024.2349451"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["And, during ",["Australia’s 2025 federal election","https://theconversation.com/thought-the-election-campaign-was-boring-maybe-youre-just-not-on-tiktok-255847"],", the Liberal Party introduced voters to Tim Cheese, an AI-generated mouse complaining about the cost of living. There were ",["diss tracks, gaming memes","https://press-files.anu.edu.au/downloads/press/n14784/html/ch08.xhtml"]," and deliberately chaotic videos, presumably designed to speak the language of a younger audience."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is the world of brainrot: nonsensical, overstimulating internet content featuring everything from AI-generated animals to surreal characters speaking in strange voices."]},{"k":"p","s":["Italian brainrot involves bizarre AI-generated creatures with pseudo-Italian names, such as a crocodile crossed with a fighter jet named Bombardino Crocodilo. But add a political message and it gets very odd."]},{"k":"p","s":["The logic is understandable. Young people spend considerable time consuming short-form entertainment, so ",["political parties want to appear in those feeds","https://doi.org/10.1177/1329878X261501254"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But there’s a fine line between understanding internet culture and looking like someone’s dad attempting a TikTok dance at Christmas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Germany’s election gets even stranger"]},{"k":"p","s":["If Australia’s experiments seem unusual, Germany’s 2025 federal election provides some competition."]},{"k":"p","s":["A youth political group affiliated with the left-wing party Die Linke turned speeches by veteran politician Gregor Gysi into techno remixes, creating the unlikely phenomenon of DJ Gysi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Die Linke subsequently won ",["25% of the vote among 18–24-year-olds","https://www1.wdr.de/nachrichten/wahlergebnis-bundestagswahl-afd-linke-social-media-tiktok-100.html?"],". Whether the techno helped is not clear."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the other side of politics, the Alternative for Germany (AfD) Brandenberg branch posted a fully AI-generated advertisement depicting the future of Germany. This video included AI versions of rival party leaders Karl Lauterbach (Social Democratic Party) and Robert Habeck (Greens)."]},{"k":"p","s":["And ",["AI-generated influencers","https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-ai-influencers-targeting-german-elections/video-71514325"]," have begun spruiking political messages. This includes ",["Larissa Wagner","https://x.com/LarissaWagt"],", who is believed to have been created by a far-right group with connections to the American online magazine Compact."]},{"k":"p","s":["A TikTok creator also used the absurdist trend of talking AI animals to question the apparent contradiction between AfD leader Alice Weidel’s personal life and her party’s policies."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s political commentary delivered by a pigeon in a bathroom. And somehow, that makes perfect sense on TikTok."]},{"k":"p","s":[["German academic Marcus Bösch","https://tiktoktiktoktiktok.substack.com/p/brainrot-as-anti-content"]," argues brainrot isn’t simply meaningless entertainment. Its absurdity can make political messages easier to circulate, often disguised through humour and irony."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s a little like hiding the vegetables in a toddler’s dinner, except the vegetables are political ideology and the dinner is an AI-generated pigeon."]},{"k":"p","s":["The danger is that repeated exposure can make even troubling political imagery appear familiar, without anyone necessarily engaging with the ideas behind it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Politics has entered the rave"]},{"k":"p","s":["Britain’s Greens party has taken the word “party” literally, moving political campaigning onto actual dance floors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since January, a grassroots collective called ",["Green Space","https://www.greenspace.community/parties"],", created by Greens members, has been organising political raves, complete with DJs, dancefloors and appearances from party leader Zack Polanski."]},{"k":"p","s":["Its first London event attracted around 1,400 revellers and raised £13,000 (A$25,000), while a ",["subsequent Leeds rave","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/apr/20/greens-zack-polanski-rave-club-night-appearance-leeds"]," drew more than 2,000 and is estimated to have raised £16,000 (A$31,000). That is considerably more tangible than a few thousand video views."]},{"k":"p","s":["It also highlights an important distinction. A nightclub fundraiser can create community, recruit volunteers and generate money, particularly in a world where we are ",["craving real connection","https://doi.org/10.1177/1329878X261472218"],", both face-to-face and virtually."]},{"k":"h","s":["When the meme becomes the message"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political parties are increasingly trying to inhabit a world, described by journalist and social commentator Kieran Press-Reynolds as “ ",["Shitpostmodernism","https://spikeartmagazine.com/articles/essay-shitpostmodernism"],"”. It is an internet of fragmented trends, absurd humour and rapidly changing cultural references."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of course, there’s nothing wrong with politicians having fun. ",["Humour can make politics","https://doi.org/10.1177/1329878X251327232"]," more accessible, while engaging with online culture can reach people who would never attend a traditional political event."]},{"k":"p","s":["But visibility, engagement and influence are very different things. Someone might share a politician’s Minecraft performance because they love it, hate it, or simply cannot believe it’s happening. None necessarily translates into a vote."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps Victorian Labor’s Minecraft party introduced politics to an entirely new audience. Or perhaps 200 people just enjoyed some phonk while a politician enthusiastically pressed buttons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Either way, the question remains: are politicians getting better at communicating with young people, or just getting better at entertaining them?"]}],"chars":5852},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/austria":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"cc0aaf3d39afc8381e69916c97a24ff0da7f974747df43eb94a4dc8944aa7949","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/austria","bytes":74710,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Austria travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:19:06+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/austria/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Austria set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Austrian Embassy in the UK","https://www.bmeia.gv.at/en/austrian-embassy-london/about-us/map-and-opening-hours/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Austria follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport if you need to","https://www.gov.uk/apply-renew-passport"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel without a visa to the Schengen area, which includes Austria, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The requirements for ",["working in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-austria-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Schengen countries within the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Austrian border control, you may need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel booking confirmation or proof of address for a second home"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your travel insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Austrian government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Austrian Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://www.bmeia.gv.at/en/travel-stay/entrance-and-residence-in-austria/"]," or the ",["Austrian Embassy in the UK","https://www.bmeia.gv.at/en/austrian-embassy-london/travelling-to-austria/entry-requirements-visa-and-immigration/schengen-visa-application-requirements/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Austria with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-austria#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border controls at Germany’s land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are temporary border controls in place to travel into Germany. Check the ",["entry requirements for Germany","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Austria","https://www.bmf.gv.at/en/topics/customs/travellers/entry-from-non-eu-countries.html"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Austria."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["national and international transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["music, sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["entertainment establishments and nightlife venues"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings and international institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship and religious sites"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should be vigilant in public places and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent examples include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 15 February 2025, one person was killed and five injured in central Villach, Carinthia, southern Austria in a knife attack"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 2 November 2020, four people were killed and 23 injured in a terrorism-related shooting in central Vienna"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Austrian authorities have successfully disrupted various attack plans, making a number of arrests in recent years. You can expect to see an increased police presence, and additional safety measures may be in place. Be aware of your surroundings and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations may happen with little or no warning in cities. Follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are generally low. However, there are higher levels of petty crime, particularly pickpocketing, in the big city centres and city parks after dark. Thieves use a variety of methods to distract people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care on public transport and in crowded city centres, including main stations. Be particularly careful with your belongings on international trains and when you take your baggage from trains and coaches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinks served in bars overseas are often stronger than those in the UK. Be careful about taking drinks from strangers or leaving your drinks unattended. Criminals have robbed and assaulted people after spiking their drinks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["By law, you must always have easy access to your passport. If you do not carry your passport, you must be able to get it quickly. It can be helpful to carry a copy of the photo page. The Austrian authorities do not accept a UK driving licence as official ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Austria have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Face-covering ban"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s generally illegal to wear any clothing or object in public that covers your face. You could get a fine of up to 150 euros. See ",["information on Austria’s face-covering ban","https://www.oesterreich.gv.at/en/themen/menschen_aus_anderen_staaten/aufenthalt/Seite.120251"],", including a list of exemptions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must validate your ticket in a ticket machine before starting a journey on public transport. If you do not, you could get a 100 to 500 euro on-the-spot fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["For outdoor activities and adventure sports, make sure:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you use a well-established company"]},{"k":"li","s":["your insurance covers your specific activity"]},{"k":"p","s":["For sports activities like skiing, potholing and mountaineering, and for sports classed as particularly dangerous (for example, off-piste skiing, mountain biking, climbing or paragliding), your insurance should include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mountain rescue services"]},{"k":"li","s":["helicopter costs"]},{"k":"li","s":["repatriation to your country of residence"]},{"k":"li","s":["transfer to neighbouring countries for treatment"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check weather forecasts and conditions. Make sure you’re properly equipped for the worst-case scenario with items such as a map, compass, GPS and telecommunications equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Adventure sports and activities are riskier if you’re alone. Consider hiring a guide for expert advice. Always leave details of your itinerary with someone."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Skiing"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["preparing for winter sports abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/winter-sports-stay-safe-on-the-slopes"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take advice on weather and avalanche conditions before you travel. Follow local skiing laws and regulations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Off-piste skiing is very dangerous and can invalidate your travel insurance. Avalanches are a risk in some areas. Follow safety instructions carefully and go with a qualified guide. See ",["European Avalanche Warning Service","https://www.avalanches.org/"]," and the Austrian Avalanche Warning Service (in German)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Austria, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Austria guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/austria/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving laws in Austria can be complex, especially for caravan and motorhomes. For more information, see EU road rules and safety and ",["Austrian vehicle laws","https://www.oesterreich.gv.at/en/themen/mobilitaet/kfz/10"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Austria if you are aged 18 or over. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Austria, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience and a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry insurance and vehicle ownership documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on driving if you’re living in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-austria#driving-in-austria"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Motorway tolls"]},{"k":"p","s":["All vehicles on motorways and expressways in Austria are subject to tolls. If you use Austrian motorways, you must ",["display a vignette (sticker)","https://www.austria.info/en/service-and-facts/getting-there-around/by-car/vignette"]," inside your windscreen. You could get a fine if you do not."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Austria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/16/austria#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Austria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/16/austria#General_Information"],", including tick-borne diseases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Austria. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/austria-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Austria, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-austria#healthcare"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance or rescue: 144"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 122"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 133"]},{"k":"p","s":["European emergency number: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also download the ",["112 Where Are U app","https://where.areu.lombardia.it/"],", the European emergency number app."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=Austria&serviceType=lawyers"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Austria"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters"]," in Austria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guide-for-austria"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/austria-prisoner-pack-austrian-prison-rules/information-pack-for-british-nationals-arrested-or-detained-in-austria"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/austria/british-embassy-vienna"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/austria/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-austria"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":16632,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/whats-missing-from-election-promises-in-victorias-rural-health-debate-a-long-term-vision-294358":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"f33cafc3de11a1fddd03fcc78e836962c62c6262d4c1bc2dfe2d354e2b4f58b1","read":"https://theconversation.com/whats-missing-from-election-promises-in-victorias-rural-health-debate-a-long-term-vision-294358","bytes":186538,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What’s missing from election promises in Victoria’s rural health debate? A long-term vision","by":[{"n":"Belinda O'Sullivan","r":"Professor and Director of Research, Monash Rural Health, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T04:15:11Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Some of Victoria’s ",["fastest-growing communities","https://www.infrastructurevictoria.com.au/topics/regional-victoria"]," are in regional areas. About ",["1.6 million people","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/population/regional-population"]," already call regional Victoria home. With ",["data centres","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-01-22/keppel-data-centre-latrobe-valley/106123748"]," and ",["major renewable energy projects","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-15/warracknabeal-wind-farm-clears-victorian-approvals/107263312"]," slated for development across the state, this number is set to grow further."]},{"k":"p","s":["A growing population will place increasing demands on already strained rural health-care services. People in these communities have a breadth of health needs, and we need preventative, primary health care and hospital care that works for all of them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unfortunately, that isn’t the reality on the ground, something which has become a key issue ahead of Victoria’s state election."]},{"k":"p","s":["In February, the Rural Doctor’s Association of Victoria ",["called on","https://rdav.com.au/VIC/_Vic/News/Vic-Articles/Fair%20deal%20urged%20for%20rural%20patients%20in%20state%20election.aspx"]," Victoria’s major parties to commit to ending the state’s “inequitable health system”."]},{"k":"p","s":["And late last month, Victorian doctors ",["demanded","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/dont-get-sick-in-vic-doctors-launch-election-campaign-targeting-broken-health-system/news-story/641c145c6b0fb3635a98d068367d054c"]," all parties fix the state’s broken health system, launching their “Don’t get sick in Vic” campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, just over two weeks out from polling day, major parties are offering only short-term and simplistic solutions, without any real overarching strategy to improve health care for rural communities. Here’s why – and what practical, lasting solutions could look like."]},{"k":"h","s":["The postcode problem"]},{"k":"p","s":["The challenges facing rural Victoria reflect a nationwide problem. Despite paying the same taxes, where Australians live can make a significant difference to the quality of health care they receive."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to an October ",["report","https://www.ruralhealth.org.au/publication/the-forgotten-health-spend-a-report-on-the-expenditure-deficit-in-rural-australia-2026/"]," by the National Rural Health Alliance, Australians living outside major cities receive about A$1,200 less per person per year across health, disability and aged-care spending."]},{"k":"p","s":["The health system in rural Victoria has yet to recover from the COVID pandemic. The loss of migratory health workers led to significant pressures on general practices and allied health businesses."]},{"k":"p","s":["The funding and training of general practitioners (GPs) is primarily the responsibility of the federal government. But GPs play a major role in the health of rural Victorians, crossing over into disability, aged care and rural hospitals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many GPs are choosing to ",["retire","https://www.racgp.org.au/getmedia/80c8bdc9-8886-4055-8a8d-ea793b088e5a/Health-of-the-Nation.pdf"]," early. Those who have remained are more selective about their workloads. A ",["2024 study","https://www1.racgp.org.au/ajgp/2024/supplement-december/burnout-and-retention-of-general-practice-supervis"]," of Australian GP supervisors suggested almost 80% have high exhaustion rates."]},{"k":"p","s":["A separate ",["2025 Australian survey","https://gpsa.org.au/research-and-policy/2025-national-survey-report/"]," found less than half (44%) said they were willing to supervise trainee doctors in the next ",["five","https://gpsa.org.au/research-and-policy/2025-national-survey-report/"]," years. This may limit how many new doctors can be trained in rural Victoria."]},{"k":"p","s":["Election promises purporting to boost rural doctor numbers – such as health worker ",["incentive schemes","https://vic.nationals.org.au/media-releases/jade-benham-mp-nationals-and-liberals-set-to-boost-regional-health-workforce/"]," – do not address how we keep them once training is over."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why promising more hospital beds alone isn’t enough"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ahead of the Victorian state election, both ",["Labor","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-25/vic-labor-campaign-launch-health-hospital-investment/107304732"]," and the ",["Coalition","https://www.vicliberal.org.au/article/strengthen-our-health-system"]," have pledged a mix of more timely emergency services, surgery, beds and health workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such promises centre on acute care, but do little to shift the dial for rural health unless they are paired with investment in grassroots general health care."]},{"k":"p","s":["In many smaller communities – particularly where access to specialist doctors is limited or requires lengthy travel – rural generalists play a vital role. These are GPs with extra training to provide complementary care across emergency, obstetrics, anaesthetics, paediatrics and palliative care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Interestingly, despite declining interest in specialising in general practice, there has been ",["growing interest","https://www.racgp.org.au/health-of-the-nation-2026/future-workforce/gps-in-training#:%7E:text=In%202025%2C%20only%208.8%25%20of%20medical%20students,for%20future%20practice%20ranks%20fourth%20(Figure%2041)"]," among medical students to specialise as a rural generalist since 2021."]},{"k":"p","s":["This presents a significant opportunity. Victoria already co-invests in the federal government’s ",["rural generalist training program","https://www.vicruralgeneralist.com.au/"],". The state could capitalise further by exploring how to create attractive and sustainable employment options for rural generalists in rural hospitals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Breaking down barriers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drawing on interviews with people involved in training and employing rural generalist doctors across Victoria, my own ",["previous research","https://doi.org/10.1111/ajr.70019"]," has examined what helps attract rural generalists to regional areas, and what makes them stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["We found several barriers. These included health services competing for a limited number of doctors, competition with other specialists, varying levels of support from hospital leaders, and problems with workforce planning."]},{"k":"p","s":["But we also identified promising solutions, including having a clear statewide plan for the rural workforce, improving coordination between different regional health services, and improving recognition and pay for rural generalists themselves."]},{"k":"h","s":["More specialists, closer to home"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rural generalists, however, don’t replace specialists; they complement them. Many rural Victorians with chronic conditions are being hit with ",["significant costs","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-15/vptas-regional-victoria-government-healthcare-access/107263272"]," to travel to Melbourne, not to mention the time lost travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["This points to the need to invest in more rural specialist training in our regions, to grow more specialists closer to home. Any new state investment in regional specialist training positions would build on the work of rural clinical schools."]},{"k":"p","s":["These institutions, with Commonwealth support, ",["select and train people from rural areas","https://doi.org/10.1111/medu.14069"]," to realise their dream of working in their own community as rural paediatricians, obstetricians and palliative care specialists. But they can’t stay if all the training is in the city."]},{"k":"h","s":["Allied health is missing from the debate"]},{"k":"p","s":["Any funding rethink should also apply to allied health and ",["multidisciplinary care","https://www.health.vic.gov.au/cancer-treatment/multidisciplinary-care"],". Allied health encompasses professionals working in a wide range of roles, including physios, occupational therapists, psychologists, speech pathologists and social workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["It has a central role keeping people moving, thinking and socially engaged. Delivered well, it also helps prevent avoidable hospital readmissions and facilitates better care for staying healthy at home, along with promoting early discharge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional Victoria currently faces a chronic deficit in rural allied health professionals and care coordinators. This is compounded by declining volunteerism and long waiting times for home care and aged care packages. And the consequences spill directly into our public emergency departments as bed-block and ambulance ramping."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, in this year’s election debate, allied health has hardly been mentioned as a solution to ",["emergency care and ambulance ramping","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-25/vic-labor-campaign-launch-health-hospital-investment/107304732"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["A coordinated approach to rural health"]},{"k":"p","s":["We’ll have to wait and see who forms the next Victorian state government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whoever does, perhaps the most important opportunity to improve rural health care is to build on investments by the federal government. And “go bold” on setting a vision for rural workforce and health service planning."]},{"k":"p","s":["A wide range of groups – the Rural Workforce Agency, rural Primary Health Networks, regional hospital networks and universities and colleges – can help inform this approach."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are a lot of voters living outside Melbourne. That means a big opportunity for the party with a strategic, engaged plan to improve rural health."]}],"chars":6873},"https://theconversation.com/why-quebec-separatism-is-unlikely-despite-the-parti-quebecois-election-win-295646":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"d69b7cc4038346b6c5c584d2cc3acdffb280db20e809e1b00ec0625faf0f646d","read":"https://theconversation.com/why-quebec-separatism-is-unlikely-despite-the-parti-quebecois-election-win-295646","bytes":188024,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Why Québec separatism is unlikely despite the Parti Québecois election win","by":[{"n":"Gavin Furrey","r":"Assistant Professor, Political Science, Université du Québec à Montréal (UQAM)"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T14:31:48Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Québec’s flagship sovereignist party, ",["the Parti Québecois (PQ), formed a minority government","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crly09gz7ew4o"]," in the recent provincial election. The party essentially rose from the dead after a 12-year absence, dethroning the right-wing nationalist — but not separatist — Coalition Avenir Québec (CAQ)."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Canadians, the PQ is typically associated with sovereignty referendums. Yet, despite the PQ victory, ",["estimates place Québecois support for sovereignty at between 27 and 31 per cent","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/montreal/quebec-parti-quebecois-electoral-reform-9.7373016"],", a far cry from the ",["49.42 per cent who voted to separate in the 1995 referendum","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2025/10/27/30-years-quebec-referendum-1995/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This figure aligns somewhat with the popular vote received by the PQ, which, at 28 per cent, is ",["the lowest popular vote share of a sitting government in the history of the province","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/montreal/quebec-parti-quebecois-electoral-reform-9.7373016"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The PQ’s victory therefore should be understood in light of three factors: low public support for the PQ and for separatism, Indigenous resistance to Québec independence and a global context where statehood doesn’t necessarily shield against interference or expand diplomatic leverage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Lukewarm mood on independence"]},{"k":"p","s":["The combination of Québec’s multi-party system and its “first-past-the-post” electoral system means governments are often formed on less than a majority of the popular vote."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In six elections between 2007–2022, an average of 53.9 per cent of votes failed to translate into seats","https://www.mercedezroberge.ca/5-les-votes-perdus-un-trait-de-caractere-du-systeme-majoritaire/?utm_"],", according to electoral expert Mercédez Roberge."]},{"k":"p","s":["This explains how the separatist PQ was able to form government despite the measured lack of enthusiasm for separatism in the province."]},{"k":"p","s":["In fact, even leaving room for the possibility that leftist ",["Québec Solidaire","https://quebecsolidaire.net/"]," supporters also support independence (though the party does not necessarily prioritize it), a combination of the popular votes earned by parties that explicitly do not support independence suggests that ",["58.24 per cent of the electorate don’t want to separate from Canada.","https://www.electionsquebec.qc.ca/en/results-and-statistics/general-election-results/2026-10-05/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["PQ leader Paul St-Pierre Plamondon’s statements following his party’s victory reflects a generally lukewarm mood towards independence in the province. During his campaign, Plamondon mitigated his promise to hold a referendum during his first term by stating it wouldn’t be held while Donald Trump remained president of the United States."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the meantime, ",["Plamondon has prioritized housing and cost of living issues, and has signalled to the English-speaking community that “we’re all in the same boat.”","https://globalnews.ca/news/12090600/pq-leader-plamondon-referendum-quebec/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Plamondon’s prudence is paired with various assertions of Québec autonomy."]},{"k":"p","s":["In his first month as premier, he’s ",["antagonized the federal government by skipping the recent Canada-European Union summit","https://www.ctvnews.ca/montreal/article/quebec-premier-paul-st-pierre-plamondon-to-skip-canada-eu-summit/"],". ",["Under the CAQ, antagonism was more often directed at Québec’s increasingly ethnically and religiously diverse population","https://www.puq.ca/catalogue/themes/pensee-federaliste-contemporaine-quebec-3833.html"],". ",["Without dropping this inward-facing orientation to nation-building","https://pq.org/nouvelles/le-parti-quebecois-sengage-a-defendre-le-consensus-quebecois-sur-la-laicite/"],", the PQ’s swipes at Ottawa suggests it will return to stoking more familiar Québec-Ottawa tensions."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in a country with longstanding debates about provincial autonomy, none of this is new or indicative of separatist sentiments. The recent PQ victory is more akin to detecting a faint pulse in a terminally ill patient than a spectacular jolt back to life."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Unruly provinces? That’s what the Fathers of Confederation expected — and planned for","https://theconversation.com/unruly-provinces-thats-what-the-fathers-of-confederation-expected-and-planned-for-192306"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Changed scene from 1995"]},{"k":"p","s":["The PQ has formed a government in a situation different from 1995."]},{"k":"p","s":["Domestically, First Nations have increasingly affirmed their place in Canada’s tapestry. In 1996, the Royal Commission on Aboriginal Peoples published ",["its five-volume, 4,000-page report making 440 recommendations","https://publications.gc.ca/Pilot/LoPBdP/EB/prb9924-e.htm"],". Among them were recognizing Indigenous Peoples as ",["self-governing nations and creating Indigenous institutions","https://www.rcaanc-cirnac.gc.ca/eng/1100100014597/1572547985018"],", including an Indigenous parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2015, the Truth and Reconciliation Commission published its final report, which included ",["94 calls to action to address the harms of the residential school system and advance reconciliation across areas that include child welfare, education, health, justice and culture","https://nctr.ca/about/truth-and-reconciliation-commission-of-canada-calls-to-action/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The following year, Canada officially adopted the United Nations Declaration for the Rights of Indigenous Peoples. ",["The document became federal law in 2021","https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/declaration/about-apropos.html"],". Finally, since 1995, ",["at least 19 modern treaties have been concluded or come into effect","https://www.rcaanc-cirnac.gc.ca/eng/1677073191939/1677073214344"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It would be misleading to claim, however, that the relationship between Canadian governments and Indigenous nations has radically changed in the last 30 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plamondon’s absence from ",["the First Nations-First Ministers meeting recently held in Ottawa","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2026/10/27/indigenous-leaders-quebec-premier-skips-first-nations-meeting/"]," is an example. Québec’s minister responsible for relations with First Nations and Inuit wrote that ",["the premier’s absence was aimed at prioritizing direct nation-to-nation meetings with Indigenous nations on “notre territoire","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2026/10/27/indigenous-leaders-quebec-premier-skips-first-nations-meeting/"]," (‘our territory.’)”"]},{"k":"p","s":["This phrasing takes Québec’s territorial sovereignty as a given, treating it as a non-negotiable precondition that other nations must accept before dialogue can even begin. By prioritizing provincial self-determination, it implicitly subordinates Indigenous sovereignty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Claiming these talks are “nation-to-nation” rings hollow when one party unilaterally dictates the terms of engagement."]},{"k":"p","s":["The premier’s decision to skip the meeting was ",["criticized by the Assembly of First Nations of Québec and Labrador (AFNQL) and the Native Women’s Shelter of Montréal","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2026/10/27/indigenous-leaders-quebec-premier-skips-first-nations-meeting/"],", who wanted Québec to be at the table in Ottawa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plamondon would do well to remember that in 1995, ",["multiple First Nations within Québec’s boundaries refused forcible inclusion into a new independent state","https://publications.gc.ca/Collection-R/LoPBdP/BP/bp412-e.htm#:%7E:text=The%20Crees%20have%20asserted%20for,keep%20their%20territory%20in%20Canada."],", notably those whose rivers provide ",["the bulk of the province’s hydroelectricity","https://nunatsiaq.com/stories/article/did-you-know-fast-facts-about-the-james-bay-hydroelectric-project/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Modern risks of independent statehood"]},{"k":"p","s":["Internationally, ",["separatist sentiments today have more to do with populism","https://theconversation.com/in-alberta-far-right-populism-fuelled-by-conspiracy-theories-and-alienation-drive-bid-to-separate-from-canada-294374"]," than with the decolonization efforts that played out in the second half of the 20th century. In a climate of ",["survival-of-the-fittest foreign policy","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmly016ep243o"],", sovereignty in the form of an independent state does not guarantee the same freedoms or capacities it might have in 1980 and 1995."]},{"k":"p","s":["As U.K. political scientist ",["Michael Keating suggests, self-determination is no longer fixed to a single people or territory","https://doi.org/10.1080/17449057.2019.1585093"],". Nations today are largely regarded as contested constructs, and territories are multi-layered with various cultural and ethnic populations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Additionally, sovereignty doesn’t shield a state from the decisions of another, as recent American tariff policies are showing Canadians all too well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["3 ways Canada can navigate an increasingly erratic and belligerent United States","https://theconversation.com/3-ways-canada-can-navigate-an-increasingly-erratic-and-belligerent-united-states-276035"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Keating’s argument aligns with ",["Indigenous political theories of relational autonomy","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319456880_What_is_a_treaty_On_contract_and_mutual_aid"],": today sovereignty is experienced less as something a nation possesses and more as a continuously negotiated relationship."]},{"k":"p","s":["American threats to Canadian sovereignty and Greenland’s self-determination suggests that secession would not necessarily improve upon Québec’s ability to negotiate its position within the broader international order."]},{"k":"p","s":["In short, in a world where even ",["the U.S., a superpower for decades, is experiencing the costs of fractured relationships","https://doi.org/10.53532/ss.038.04.00129"],", a convincing pitch for Québec separatism would have to take into account similar costs. The pulse of Québec separatism persists, though the body sustaining it is weighed down by internal fractures and a punishing political landscape."]}],"chars":7164},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/gabon":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"39553974335cc9e9b95992b7ccf59d4fd744e26a8bfd6370de3153aad3732a60","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/gabon","bytes":47667,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Gabon travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-06T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2025-12-10T13:37:09+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/gabon/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Gabon’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Gabon set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Gabon High Commission on 020 7823 9986 or email gabonembassyuk@gmail.com."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ that is at least 6 months after the date you arrive in Gabon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Gabon."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must apply for a visa before travelling. For more information on the visa application process, contact the ",["Gabon High Commission in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"]," on 020 7823 9986 or email gabonembassyuk@gmail.com."]},{"k":"p","s":["The most reliable way to get a visa is through the High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["For business travel, you must provide a letter of invitation from an individual or company in Gabon explaining the reason for your trip."]},{"k":"p","s":["For tourist travel, you must provide a hotel booking or letter from your hotel confirming your stay."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Gabon, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Gabon guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/84/gabon#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Gabon","https://douanes.ga/individuals/traveler-s-guide"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Gabon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Gabon, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Presidential elections will be held on 12 April, 2025, in Gabon. We do not expect significant disruption, however British Nationals should continue to exercise vigilance in crowded areas and near polling stations, and avoid rallies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and unrest can occur without warning and the situation could change quickly. During periods of unrest, police checks may increase. Make sure you have all required documentation with you and avoid large gatherings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Borders have reopened following the military takeover in August 2023, but some disruption may happen. Contact your travel provider for more information and follow instructions from local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the local authorities and your travel provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media and follow any curfew restrictions"]},{"k":"li","s":["remain vigilant and stay indoors where possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid protests or large gatherings and any military activity"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Detention of tourists"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political and security tensions following the August 2023 military coup resulted in some tourists being held and questioned about their reasons for travelling to Gabon. Some individuals had their passports taken and were briefly prevented from leaving the country. While the situation has stabilised, current political and security sensitivities mean that the authorities may treat tourists with heightened scrutiny."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests in Gabon are not common but happen on occasion and may turn violent without warning. You should avoid all demonstrations and rallies and remain vigilant during periods of unrest."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of robbery, armed attacks and rape in Gabon."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can take steps to reduce your risk and help protect your belongings, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoiding remote areas, particularly after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["being cautious on quiet or isolated beaches around Libreville, and avoiding them at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wearing expensive jewellery or carrying large amounts of cash"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping smartphones and other electronic items out of sight"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping car windows shut and doors locked"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxis in Gabonese cities operate like buses, picking up more passengers if there is room in the car. They often take indirect routes. There have been reports of violent assaults and robberies on taxi passengers. Use licensed taxis, and ask to book the taxi exclusively so it does not pick up other passengers. Check with your tour operator or travel provider if they have a taxi service you can use."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Carjacking"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of carjackings in Libreville. If you’re a victim of an attack, stay calm and surrender your valuables and your vehicle if asked. Do not resist."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check your route for any hazards or disruptions before you set off"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep to main roads and park in well-lit areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your doors locked and windows closed while driving, especially when stopped at junctions"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid being stationary inside your vehicle for long periods"]},{"k":"li","s":["check your car is locked when you leave it"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep valuables out of sight, ideally in the boot"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not pick up strangers"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money and credit card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit cards are not widely accepted except at hotels. Credit card fraud is common outside the major hotel chains. Be alert when paying by card and withdrawing cash from ATMs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["By law, you need to be able to show proof of your identity to the authorities if asked. Carry your passport and visa, or a certified copy of the photo and visa pages of your passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of drugs is a serious offence and punishment can be severe, including a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photography of government and military buildings and airports is illegal and may lead to arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal. There are no laws against discrimination on the grounds of sexual orientation. Gabon remains a conservative society and discrimination can be a problem for those open about their sexual identity. Same-sex marriage is not recognised in Gabon."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Gabon, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions in Gabon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions in the centre of Libreville are generally good. Conditions in local inland areas are poor and driving can be hazardous. During the rainy season from October to mid-December and mid-February to May, many roads are passable only with a 4-wheel-drive vehicle. Avoid travelling by road at night as many roads are unlit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Official checkpoints are common. Police will ask for your passport, driving licence and vehicle registration documents. See more ",["information on drivers being stopped by police","https://www.legigabon.com/single-post/2019/02/15/TOUT-SAVOIR-SUR-LES-CONTR%C3%94LES-ROUTIERS"]," (in French). Your car should also have a:"]},{"k":"li","s":["first aid kit"]},{"k":"li","s":["fire extinguisher"]},{"k":"li","s":["catalytic converter"]},{"k":"li","s":["warning triangle"]},{"k":"li","s":["torch"]},{"k":"li","s":["set of wheel chocks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["British government employees do not use domestic flights run by Gabonese airline companies unless this is unavoidable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pirates have carried out armed attacks on commercial shipping vessels in the Gulf of Guinea. Take extreme care when travelling in coastal waters."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling by sea, ",["read about the regional risks at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 117, 1300, 011760873 or 1333 and ask for an ambulance. Operators may only speak French."]},{"k":"p","s":["These numbers are not always reliable. Emergency help can be limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Gabon","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/84/gabon#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Gabon","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/84/gabon"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"hs","s":["HIV and AIDS"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Joint United Nations Programme on HIV/AIDS (UNAIDS) estimates that around 44,000 adults aged 15 or over in Gabon are living with HIV; the prevalence percentage is estimated at 3.8% of the adult population compared with the prevalence percentage in adults in the UK of around 0.2%. You should take normal precautions to avoid exposure to HIV/AIDS."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Gabon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are limited, particularly in rural areas. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Gabon","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/gabon-medical-providers"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Gabon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 117. Depending on your mobile network, call: 1300, 0174 or 0880 for SOS Médecins. Operators may only speak French."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 177"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 177"]},{"k":"p","s":["None of these numbers are guaranteed to be reliable. Emergency help can be limited in some places that are hard to reach"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Gabon"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Gabon"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Gabon"]," in Gabon"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Gabon","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-national-dies-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Gabon","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/gabon-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/gabon/british-high-commission-yaounde"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/gabon/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":12441,"change":"New information about dual nationals returning to the UK (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-macedonia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"4fb2fdfb891b891bbff0211cc7a8e740e1f6b27fa1a86243af4d83a0e96e2b20","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/north-macedonia","bytes":57489,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"North Macedonia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-13T16:16:47+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel disruption"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area. The EES may take each passenger extra time, so it is important to be prepared to wait longer than usual at EU country borders and allow more time for immigration controls if travelling to and from the Schengen area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-macedonia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in North Macedonia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Macedonian Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.gov.mk/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter North Macedonia, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 90 days after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit North Macedonia for up to 3 months without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay for longer, contact the ",["Macedonian Embassy","https://london.mfa.gov.mk/en"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel, ask your airline if you need to complete any forms for children travelling:"]},{"k":"li","s":["alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["with only one parent"]},{"k":"li","s":["with an adult who is not their legal guardian"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling through (transiting) other countries, check travel advice for those countries for additional requirements."]},{"k":"hs","s":["UK refugee travel documents"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hold a UK refugee travel document, you must have a visa to travel to North Macedonia. You also need a visa to travel through North Macedonia on your way to Kosovo. You can apply for a visa from the ",["Macedonian Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.gov.mk/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the police"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must register with the local police in the town or city where you’re staying within 48 hours of your arrival in North Macedonia. If you’re staying in a hotel, staff will register you at check-in."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep the registration document with you until you leave North Macedonia. If you have registered with the police directly, you must de-register 24 hours before you leave the country. You can ",["register with the police online","https://mvr.gov.mk/prijavistrintro"]," (in Macedonian)."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not register, you may face:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a fine"]},{"k":"li","s":["detention and a court hearing"]},{"k":"li","s":["a restriction on returning to North Macedonia"]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling to Serbia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Serbia has sometimes denied entry to people leaving North Macedonia with passport stamps from Kosovo."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s North Macedonia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/133/north-macedonia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of North Macedonia","https://customs.gov.mk/en-GB/pocetna/fizicki-lica/patnici/stoka-bez-uvozni-davacki.nspx"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into North Macedonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare foreign currency if the value is 10,000 euros or more when you enter North Macedonia. If you do not, customs officers may detain you and seize the cash when you try to leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in North Macedonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in North Macedonia cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Stay aware of your surroundings and keep up to date with local media reports and follow advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in North Macedonia have carried out raids against suspected terrorists. There’s a risk of terrorist attacks inspired by extremist ideology in North Macedonia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Occasionally there are protests which can cause disruption. Check local media for the latest information, be vigilant and avoid large crowds and gatherings."]},{"k":"p","s":["If there is civil disorder, stay indoors when possible, especially after dark, and avoid crowds and demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks against foreign nationals are extremely rare."]},{"k":"p","s":["Organised crime groups are active, particularly in northern areas near the border with Kosovo."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasional shooting incidents, including in Skopje, but they are not targeted at foreign nationals. People sometimes fire guns when celebrating."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several cases of pickpocketing by gangs of children and bag snatching in the main shopping and entertainment areas late at night. Foreign nationals appear to have been specifically targeted. Make sure your personal possessions are secure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your passport in a safe place and carry a copy of the photo page for identification. If it is lost or stolen, report it to the local police and ",["cancel your passport immediately","https://www.gov.uk/report-a-lost-or-stolen-passport"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in North Macedonia have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photographs of any military installation or site of government or strategic importance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual relationships are legal, but people in North Macedonia are not particularly open about them. LGBT+ bars and restaurants are not common. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["British banks do not exchange Macedonian denars, so exchange any unwanted denars before you leave. You should only change money through banks or official exchanges and not through street dealers. You will not be able to exchange Scottish or Northern Irish banknotes."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in North Macedonia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s North Macedonia guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/macedonia/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of. You can get fines for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not using side lights or dipped headlights, including during the day"]},{"k":"li","s":["using a mobile phone while driving"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wearing a seatbelt, as both a driver and a passenger"]},{"k":"li","s":["not having all the required safety equipment, including snow chains where conditions require them"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in North Macedonia. Unless you’re driving a rental car or have a residence permit, you’ll also need to have the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],". You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as at least 2 years of driving experience and a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have an accident, do not move your vehicle until the police record the incident and allow you to move. In case of emergency, contact:"]},{"k":"li","s":["police: 192"]},{"k":"li","s":["ambulance: 194"]},{"k":"li","s":["roadside assistance: 196"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in North Macedonia. If you are tested and found to have 50 milligrams of alcohol per 100 millilitres of blood (England’s limit is 80mg per 100ml), you may get a heavy fine and possible imprisonment. If you’re a professional driver (for example, an HGV driver), any alcohol in your system can lead to arrest and a heavy fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling on major roads, you can pay the toll in Macedonian denars or in euros with cash or a credit card."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards and road conditions vary widely. Driving styles differ significantly from those in UK. Accidents are common. Always take care while driving or on foot."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving a British car in North Macedonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are taking your own car, you must have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicle registration"]},{"k":"li","s":["ownership documents"]},{"k":"li","s":["valid insurance to drive in North Macedonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check your insurance covers you to drive in North Macedonia and you are able to show proof to border officials. A green card might be helpful to demonstrate you have the correct cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Delays for lorries at borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lorries crossing the North Macedonia border may be subject to long delays. Make sure you have the proper customs documentation before you arrive at the border."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["From November to February there can be thick fog in Skopje and surrounding areas. There can be flight delays and diversions if fog affects visibility at Skopje airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can find flight information on the ",["Skopje International Airport","https://skp.airports.com.mk/en-EN/"]," website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are possible in North Macedonia from April to October due to the dry and hot weather. Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when visiting or driving through countryside"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure cigarette ends are properly extinguished"]},{"k":"li","s":["not light fires or barbecues except in designated and marked areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leave any rubbish"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government commonly introduces a ban on entering forest and wilderness areas during summer months when the risk of wildfires is highest. Fines for non-compliance are severe. For further information seek local advice or contact Public Enterprise National Forests."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see a wildfire, call the emergency services on 112. Follow any advice from the police or local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes occur occasionally. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 194 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the latest information on vaccinations and health risks in ",["TravelHealthPro’s North Macedonia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/133/north-macedonia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in North Macedonia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/133/north-macedonia"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["West Nile virus and other mosquito-borne diseases"]},{"k":"li","s":["air pollution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of North Macedonia. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in North Macedonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a reciprocal healthcare agreement for British nationals, which entitles you to ",["free emergency treatment in North Macedonia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-reciprocal-healthcare-agreements-with-non-eu-countries#north-macedonia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate insurance. You may need to pay before getting some treatment. Familiarise yourself with your travel insurance policy and what it covers."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in North Macedonia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/north-macedonia-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in North Macedonia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 194"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 192"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roadside assistance: 196"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=North%20Macedonia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=North%20Macedonia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=North%20Macedonia"]," in North Macedonia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in North Macedonia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/when-someone-dies-in-north-macedonia"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in North Macedonia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/north-macedonia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/north-macedonia/british-embassy-skopje"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/north-macedonia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in North Macedonia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-north-macedonia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":14513,"change":"New information on wait times if travelling to and from the Schengen area from North Macedonia ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"ace543187030dcab7cf590fa01079dffbfd9d113e335c04d5af3b8076f34c44d","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria","bytes":117403,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Nigeria travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-19T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-10T14:13:23+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["North East Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Borno State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yobe State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Adamawa State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Gombe State"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bauchi State"]},{"k":"hs","s":["North West Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Katsina State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zamfara State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sokoto State"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kaduna State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kano State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kebbi State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Jigawa State"]},{"k":"hs","s":["North Central Nigeria and the Federal Capital Territory, including Abuja"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Niger State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kogi State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Plateau State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Taraba State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kwara State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Benue State"]},{"k":"hs","s":["South East and South South Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the riverine areas (the river and swamp locations accessible by boat, but not by road) of Delta, Bayelsa, Rivers, Akwa Ibom and Cross River states."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Abia State"]},{"k":"li","s":["non-riverine areas of Delta, Bayelsa, and Rivers States"]},{"k":"li","s":["Anambra State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Imo State"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Nigeria’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Nigeria set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Nigeria High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Nigeria, your passport must have an expiry date at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Nigeria as a visitor. Get your visa before travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a valid Nigerian residence permit (CERPAC or Green Card), you do not need a visa to enter Nigeria."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information contact the Nigeria High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Visa on arrival is no longer available. All visa applications must be submitted through the online portal prior to travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["apply for a visa from Nigerian Immigration Services","https://portal.immigration.gov.ng/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Landing and departure cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Nigerian authorities have introduced a system for foreigners to complete landing and departure cards before entry/exit and you may be asked for these at the airport or other border points."]},{"k":"p","s":["The forms can be completed through the ",["online portal","https://lecard.immigration.gov.ng/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Nigeria, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see TravelHealthPro’s Nigeria guide."]},{"k":"p","s":["Infants aged 8 months or younger and adults aged 61 or older are exempt from this requirement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["Additional screening for Ebola (Bundibugyo Virus) Disease is in place at border entry points into Nigeria. International travellers must complete an online ",["Nigeria Health Declaration Form","https://healthapp.ncdc.gov.ng/"]," before travel. You may also be required to undergo thermal screening and a travel history check on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before crossing by land between Nigeria and Benin, Niger or Cameroon, check with the relevant border and immigration authorities that your crossing point is open and check the current entry and exit requirements. Read the travel advice for both countries and the regional risks advice for your whole route. An open border crossing does not mean the journey is safe or that FCDO advice against travel no longer applies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Nigeria","https://customs.gov.ng/?page_id=3075"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import beer, mineral water, soft drinks, sparkling wine, fruits, vegetables, cereals, eggs, textile fabrics, jewellery or precious metals."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to export African art, particularly antiques, without written authorisation from the Department of Antiquities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["regional risks advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Nigeria."]},{"k":"p","s":["The primary terrorist threat in Nigeria comes from Islamic State West Africa (ISWA) and Boko Haram. These groups are mainly based in north-east Nigeria in Borno, Yobe and Adamawa states. In recent years, there have also been attacks likely associated with terrorist groups in the following states: Borno, Gombe, Niger, Kaduna, Kogi, Bauchi, Ondo, Zamfara, Taraba, Jigawa, Sokoto, Edo and Kano states, as well as the Federal Capital Territory."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate and could occur at any time, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["markets"]},{"k":"li","s":["malls"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["bars and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["sports venues and screenings"]},{"k":"li","s":["displacement camps"]},{"k":"li","s":["train networks and stations"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["educational institution"]},{"k":"li","s":["international organisations"]},{"k":"li","s":["large public gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["military locations and venues within them"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care during election periods, or periods of religious significance or other public holidays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist groups have also constructed unauthorised vehicle checkpoints on major supply and commercial routes, such as the A3 Maiduguri-Damaturu Road."]},{"k":"p","s":["A heavy security presence is often a sign of a particularly high risk. Avoid affected areas in the immediate aftermath of an attack. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2025, 5 people were killed and 35 injured, in an IED attack on Maiduguri Mosque in Borno state"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2025, one soldier was killed in an attack in Kwara state. This was the first time that al-Qa’eda affiliated group JNIM have claimed an attack in Nigeria"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2025, 63 people were killed in a firearms attack in Darajamal, Borno state. Boko Haram are believed to have been responsible"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2025, 16 people were killed in a firearms attack in Morai, Kebbi state"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2024, at least 37 people were killed in an attack on Mafa town, Yobe state. ISWA claimed responsibility for the attack"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2024, 30 people were killed in coordinated suicide bombings in Gwoza, Borno state"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist groups are highly likely to carry out kidnaps in Nigeria. Kidnappings are widespread and could occur anywhere. Foreign nationals and humanitarian workers have been kidnapped in the North, including in the states of Adamawa, Bauchi, Borno, Katsina, Kano and Kebbi. There may be an increased risk of terrorist kidnap, particularly to NGO workers, in Borno State."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["When arranging meetings, use a secure location. Avoid regular patterns of travel and aim to only travel during daylight hours."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political rallies, protests and violent demonstrations can take place with little notice. Get advice on areas to avoid from local authorities, local news outlets or your travel operator. Take care if you’re visiting crowded public places or attending events which attract large crowds. If you see a threatening or intimidating situation, do not try to make your way through it. Turn around and move to safety."]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents of intercommunal violence occur frequently and often without warning throughout Nigeria. Although foreign nationals are not normally targeted, there is a risk you could be caught in an attack. Monitor local government announcements and media reporting."]},{"k":"p","s":["Widespread public demonstrations periodically take place across Nigeria including in major cities of Abuja and Lagos. Past protests have resulted in disruption, violence, and the security services have made use of tear gas, rubber bullets and live fire on occasion. Protests may occur with little notice. Exercise caution when travelling, limit travel after dark, avoid large crowds and gatherings, and monitor local media reporting, as well as UK Travel Advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Curfews and communication blackouts"]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities impose, amend and lift curfews and restrictions on the movement of vehicles at short notice throughout Nigeria."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you fail to observe curfews and restrictions, you could be at significant risk of arrest and detention. Check with the local authorities or someone with local knowledge for up-to-date information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Network operators in Nigeria have in the past been ordered to suspend mobile networks and wi-fi with very little notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Street and vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Levels of violent crime are high throughout Nigeria, including muggings, armed robbery, carjacking and kidnap."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent reports of armed robbery, carjacking and kidnap on roads across Nigeria. Risks can be higher outside major urban areas and when travelling at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Nigerian authorities, including the Federal Road Safety Corps (FRSC), have highlighted the risks associated with road travel at night. Travelling after dark can increase exposure to both security and road safety risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may target foreign nationals, including British nationals, due to their perceived wealth. Follow the advice of your host, employer or local contacts and considerlimiting unnecessary road travel after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Limit the amount of cash you carry and keep valuable items such as watches and jewellery out of sight. Stay aware of your surroundings and keep your belongings secure."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are the victim of an armed robbery, comply with the attackers’ demands and do not resist."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Withdrawing and exchanging money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals may target people withdrawing cash from banks and ATMs. Take extra care when withdrawing money, particularly after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit card fraud is common. Always keep your card within sight when making payments and regularly check your account for unauthorised transactions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Financial scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are frequently targeted by scammers operating in West Africa. Scams can take many forms, including romance and friendship scams, fraudulent business opportunities, investment schemes, inheritance claims and fake job offers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious if you receive unsolicited requests for money, investment opportunities or employment offers. Be wary of anyone you have only met online and avoid sending money or sharing personal or financial information with people you do not know."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are asked to transfer money to Nigeria on behalf of someone claiming to be a friend or relative, contact them using a trusted method to confirm the request is genuine."]},{"k":"p","s":["If someone contacts you claiming to be a British national in distress in Nigeria and requesting financial assistance, verify their identity independently."]},{"k":"p","s":["Scammers sometimes impersonate the British High Commission or other UK government organisations. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from the British High Commission in Nigeria, contact the High Commission directly using contact details published on GOV.UK or the ",["British Deputy High Commission","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-deputy-high-commission-lagos#contact-us"]," in Lagos. Please report any scams to ",["Action Fraud","https://www.reportfraud.police.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information on common scams and how to protect yourself, see GOV.UK guidance on ",["avoiding and reporting internet scams and phishing","https://www.gov.uk/report-suspicious-emails-websites-phishing"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Surrogacy and fertility treatment"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re considering fertility treatment or surrogacy options in Nigeria, exercise caution. There have been reports of staged fake births, commonly referred to as ‘miracle babies’, where visitors are falsely led to believe that a birth has taken place."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regulation of fertility treatment and surrogacy services in Nigeria is weak, and legal protections for intended parents and surrogates may be limited. There have also been reports of legal disputes involving international surrogacy arrangements in both Nigerian and English courts."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to bring a child born through fertility treatment or surrogacy in Nigeria to the UK, make sure you understand the relevant UK immigration and health requirements. See ",["Guidance on surrogacy overseas","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/surrogacy-overseas/surrogacy-overseas"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Overseas Adoption"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK has restricted overseas adoption of children from Nigeria. If you bring a child who is not biologically related to you into the UK without following the legal procedures, you could face prosecution and the child may not be eligible for British citizenship."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kidnapping for ransom"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of kidnapping across Nigeria. Kidnappings happen in both rural and urban areas, including on roads between towns and cities. British nationals could be targeted, including people travelling for work or visiting friends and relatives."]},{"k":"p","s":["The threat varies by location. Armed criminal groups carry out kidnappings in the north-west and north-central regions. There is also a high threat of kidnapping by terrorist groups in the north-east. However, kidnappings are not limited to these areas. Incidents also occur in southern Nigeria and the outer suburbs of Abuja."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read the regional risks advice for your destination and any areas you plan to travel through."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling by road:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check current security conditions along your whole route"]},{"k":"li","s":["use trusted transport providers"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan journeys to arrive before dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["vary your routes and routines where possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep up to date with local security information and follow the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not assume that major roads are safe. Travelling during daylight does not remove the risk of kidnapping."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the Niger Delta, there is a risk of kidnapping and armed attacks, including people working at oil and gas facilities and offshore installations. If you are travelling for work, check that your employer has appropriate security arrangements and emergency plans."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kidnappers may target people they believe can pay a ransom, or whose relatives or employers can pay. Criminal groups may transfer hostages to terrorist organisations. Read the ‘Terrorist kidnap’ advice alongside this section."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vary your routines and arrange meetings in secure locations. Keep up to date with local security information and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check FCDO’s travel advice before making arrangements and again before travelling. Security precautions do not make it safe to travel to areas where FCDO advises against travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Nigeria."]},{"k":"p","s":["Where incidents have been reported, Nigerian authorities have sought to shut down production centres, particularly for unlicensed traditional gin. Avoid drinking unlicensed products."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using a mobile"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your SIM must be linked to a Nigerian Identification Number. Get guidance from your network operator."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nigeria has the largest Muslim population in sub-Saharan Africa. You should behave and dress modestly, particularly in the north and when visiting religious sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year. During this time, in any predominantly Muslim area you should not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public areas (including in cars and taxis) during the daytime"]},{"k":"li","s":["sit down to eat in hotels and restaurants without checking if there is a separate or screened area for food and drink"]},{"k":"li","s":["ignore dress codes – it is more important to wear respectful clothing during Ramadan"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music, swear, shout, sing or dance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly at dusk when people are getting back home to eat."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession or use of illegal drugs, including cannabis, carries severe penalties in Nigeria. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nigeria has excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items at the border. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photography of government, military buildings and airports may lead to arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Nigeria with penalties of up to 14 years in prison. Some northern states observe Sharia Law which can prescribe the death penalty for same-sex sexual activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ‘Same Sex Marriage Prohibition Act’ provides for lengthy prison sentences for anyone involved in same-sex marriages, including those who help arrange, carry out or even attend events perceived to be same-sex weddings. The Act also criminalises anyone who helps register, organise or participate in LGBT+ groups, organisations, or those who publicly promote same-sex relationships."]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are generally viewed as socially unacceptable in Nigerian society. There is an increased risk of violence, attacks and threats, such as blackmail and intimidation against anyone being thought to be part of the LGBT+ community or supporting their rights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road travel in Nigeria can be dangerous due to poor road conditions, low driving standards and vehicles that are not roadworthy. Kidnapping, armed robbery and attacks on vehicles are also a risk. Read the regional risks advice for your destination and any areas you plan to travel through."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to drive in Nigeria, read the ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". Serious and fatal road collisions are common. Traffic congestion, particularly in Lagos, can cause long delays. Allow extra time for journeys and carry a charged mobile phone and bottled water."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Nigeria with a UK driving licence for up to 3 months. Make sure your licence is valid and ",["renew or update it","https://www.gov.uk/browse/driving/driving-licences"]," if necessary. The minimum legal driving age is 18."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay longer than 3 months, you will need a 1968 ",["international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"],". For stays of more than a year, you will need a ",["Nigerian driver’s licence","https://www.nigeriadriverslicence.org/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plan journeys outside city centres to arrive before dark and use well-lit busier roads where possible. Travelling in daylight does not remove the risk of kidnapping or armed robbery. Keep doors locked, windows closed and valuables out of sight. Stay alert in traffic jams and at traffic lights. If you think you are being followed, drive to a place of safety, such as a police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling outside cities, get current local advice on road and security conditions along your whole route. Use a trusted transport provider and check that the vehicle is roadworthy. Do not assume that travelling on major roads or in a convoy will keep you safe. Follow local restrictions and the advice of the authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dangers at road checkpoints"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are authorised and unauthorised vehicle checkpoints throughout Nigeria. Some are used for security checks, while others are used to extort money from motorists. Slow down when approaching a checkpoint and stay calm."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unauthorised checkpoints can pose a risk of robbery, kidnapping and violence. The risk varies by location. Do not assume that checkpoints in Nigeria are safe. Terrorist groups have also established checkpoints on major routes, including the A3 Maiduguri–Damaturu road in the north-east."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read the regional risks advice for your destination and any areas you plan to travel through."]},{"k":"h","s":["Taxis and buses"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of robbery and kidnapping when using taxis and public transport in Nigeria. Vehicle maintenance, insurance and driver standards vary between operators."]},{"k":"p","s":["Where possible, arrange transport in advance through a reputable hotel or trusted transport provider rather than accepting unsolicited offers of a lift. App-based taxi services do not remove the risk of crime. Before getting in, check that the driver and vehicle registration match the booking. If they do not match, do not get in. Keep the booking in the app and share your journey details with someone you trust. For long-distance bus journeys, check security conditions along the whole route and plan to travel during daylight where possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Arrange airport collections before you travel. Confirm your driver’s name, contact details and vehicle registration directly with the company or person arranging your transport. Criminals may pose as drivers or airport greeters. Do not rely only on someone knowing your name or displaying a name board. If the person or vehicle does not match the details provided, stay inside the terminal while you contact your transport provider. Airport pick-up arrangements for app-based services can vary, so check the current collection point with your provider."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Piracy, armed robbery and kidnapping for ransom remain threats in Nigerian waters and the wider Gulf of Guinea, including for people travelling to and from vessels. There is also a risk of armed attacks and kidnapping on waterways in the Niger Delta."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling by sea or river, get professional maritime security advice and check current threat information for your route. Vessel operators should follow the latest maritime security guidance."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the riverine areas of Delta, Bayelsa, Rivers, Akwa Ibom and Cross River states. Riverine areas are river and swamp locations that can be reached by boat, but not by road."]},{"k":"h","s":["Swimming risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Swimming off the coast of Nigeria can be dangerous because of rip tides and undertows. Drownings occur each year. Get local advice before swimming."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Nigeria. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Insecurity is increasing across Nigeria. Kidnapping, violent crime, and intercommunal violence occur throughout all regions of Nigeria. You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["North East Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Borno State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yobe State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Adamawa State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Gombe State"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bauchi state"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high and increasing threat from Boko Haram or Islamic State West Africa, particularly around transport hubs, religious areas and large gatherings. Humanitarian personnel, vehicles, supplies and infrastructure can be targeted by terrorists and criminals."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of kidnap and violent attacks. Intercommunal tensions can lead to outbreaks of violence. During the dry season, between March and November, when roads are more easily accessible this risk is heightened."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regular military operations are ongoing in Adamawa, Borno and Yobe states. There is a risk of retaliatory attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in the north-east against FCDO advice, keep in touch with the authorities and the wider community on the security situation. Make sure your safety procedures and contingency plans are up to date. If you are working, make sure you have confidence in your employer’s ability to extract you in the event of any emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["If in Maiduguri, be aware that if security were to deteriorate any further, it could be extremely difficult for you to leave the city. Be mindful of the risks of travelling by road in this area and take precautions."]},{"k":"h","s":["North West Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Katsina State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zamfara State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sokoto State"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kaduna State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kano State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kebbi State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Jigawa State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sokoto State"]},{"k":"p","s":["Banditry and violent attacks are frequent and there is a high threat of kidnap. Transport routes can be vulnerable to attacks by bandits and armed groups. If you’re travelling in the north-west against FCDO advice, be extremely cautious and monitor local media."]},{"k":"h","s":["North Central Nigeria and the Federal Capital Territory, including Abuja"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Niger State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kogi State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Plateau State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Taraba State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kwara State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Benue State"]},{"k":"p","s":["This advice is due to criminal and militant activity and incidents of intercommunal violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The outer suburbs of Abuja, within the Federal Capital Territory are prone to varying levels of violence, and the safety of daily activity is unpredictable. Violent crime, often involving firearms, has increased and spread from the outer suburbs to more central, wealthier areas of the city."]},{"k":"p","s":[["See Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/safety-and-security#terrorism"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious when travelling in the Federal Capital Territory. Take advice from trusted contacts and be prepared to cancel or limit your plans. British Government staff in Nigeria have been advised to restrict travel to an area broadly within the Abuja metropolitan area."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Nigerian government has warned against travelling at night in north-central Nigeria because of security concerns."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are protests in Abuja from time to time, which can turn violent. Monitor local media, avoid demonstrations and large gatherings and follow instructions from local police and security forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents of intercommunal violence and banditry frequently occur in Benue State, with a number of deaths reported. There may be increased security presence in parts of the state."]},{"k":"p","s":["There has also been an increase in violence in Kwara State, with a number of deaths reported. There may be an increased security presence in parts of the state."]},{"k":"h","s":["South East and South South Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the riverine areas (the river and swamp locations accessible by boat, but not by road) of Delta, Bayelsa, Rivers, Akwa Ibom and Cross River states."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Abia State"]},{"k":"li","s":["non-riverine areas of Delta, Bayelsa and Rivers states"]},{"k":"li","s":["Anambra State"]},{"k":"li","s":["Imo State"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk of kidnapping, armed robbery and other violent crime in the Niger Delta. Armed groups have attacked oil and gas infrastructure, and people working at or travelling to these facilities can be at risk. Threats also affect river journeys and travel to and from offshore installations. Security conditions vary by location. Check current conditions along your whole route and, if travelling for work, confirm that your employer has appropriate security arrangements and emergency plans."]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed attacks and targeted killings remain a risk in the south-east, including in towns and cities as well as on isolated roads. Police stations, checkpoints, patrols and other security facilities have been attacked, putting people nearby at risk. On 17 October 2026, an attack involving explosives on a police station in Aba, Abia State, killed two police officers. Avoid the area of an attack and follow local security instructions. Curfews and other movement restrictions may be introduced at short notice. Check current local requirements before travelling and avoid road journeys after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Violence linked to separatist activity and clashes with security forces remain risks in the south-east. Foreign nationals are not normally the intended targets of these clashes but could be caught in an attack. Improvised explosive devices have been used in the region, including in Imo State. Protests and attempts to enforce ‘sit-at-home’ restrictions can lead to violence and disrupt transport, businesses and access to services. Do not assume that reports of a new restriction or its cancellation are reliable. Check current local security information before travelling, avoid demonstrations and gatherings, and monitor official announcements and local reporting."]},{"k":"h","s":["South West Nigeria including Lagos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crimes such as mugging, kidnapping, car-jacking and armed robbery are common, particularly in the larger cities. Intercommunal violence is common and can flare up suddenly. Large-scale terrorist attacks are rare, but Islamic State West Africa claimed 2 attacks in 2022. While these attacks have not targeted foreign nationals, try to avoid being caught up in such incidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious when travelling in Lagos, particularly on the mainland, which attracts high levels of crime and where security levels can be unpredictable. Street crime is a significant risk across Lagos, particularly in crowded areas. Take sensible measures to guard your possessions and reduce your personal risk. Be cautious when moving around Lagos at night, risks can be particularly high when moving around the city by foot."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert and take any security advice given by your hotel, employer or your hosts."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 to report an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no national ambulance service and hospital-owned services are extremely limited. You may need to get local advice or arrange local transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Nigeria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/165/nigeria#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you must pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Nigeria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/165/nigeria"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 20 October 2026, the Nigerian Federal Ministry of Health and Social Welfare confirmed its first imported case of Ebola in the Federal Capital Territory and are implementing public health measures in response, including contact tracing. Follow the advice of local authorities and monitor updates from the ",["Federal Ministry of Health and Social Welfare","https://health.gov.ng/press-releases/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel to Nigeria, read ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheets/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"li","s":["You have filled in the ",["online Nigeria Health Declaration Form","https://healthapp.ncdc.gov.ng/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pharmacies are widely available in Nigeria. They will accept prescriptions from the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most medicines that require a prescription from a doctor in the UK will require one in Nigeria. If you need a new prescription, a doctor in Nigeria can issue one for a fee. Take your existing packaging to show them exactly what you need."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Nigeria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nigeria-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical standards differ from the UK and you will have to pay for any medical treatment at public hospitals. Private hospitals are more expensive. Local hospitals may be crowded and there can be shortages in medical supplies and equipment. If you need medical help in Nigeria, contact your medical insurance provider for advice on suitable healthcare facilities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Nigeria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no national ambulance service and hospital-owned services are extremely limited. You may need to get local advice or arrange local transport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Nigeria"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Nigeria"]," in Nigeria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Nigeria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-nigeria?utm_source=british-high-commission-abuja&utm_medium=embassy&utm_campaign=nigeria"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Nigeria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nigeria-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/nigeria/british-high-commission-abuja"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nigeria/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Nigeria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-nigeria"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":34685,"change":"This travel advice has been reviewed for accuracy with changes made throughout, including on land borders, street and vehicle crime, withdrawing and exchanging money, financial scams, terrorism in Nigeria, kidnapping for ransom, transport risks, dangers at road checkpoints, taxis and buses, sea trav"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palestine":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T17:20Z","sha":"1da3e7c0c58c90fc28c368ea5f2e8b9f458dc25aa5d2e8b66a95764bfcfb6c98","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/palestine","bytes":123911,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Palestine travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-05-21T11:42:53+01:00","mod":"2026-11-18T16:32:19+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Gaza"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas near Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 500m of the border with Gaza"]},{"k":"hs","s":["The West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tulkarm Governorate, Jenin Governorate, and Tubas Governorate except Route 90"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Northern Israel and Occupied Golan Heights"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Areas north of Route 89 between Nahariyya and Dalton; north of a straight eastward line from Dalton to Route 91; and north of Route 91 across the Golan Heights, excluding routes 89 and 91 themselves"]},{"k":"li","s":["Within 500m of the Area of Separation in the occupied Golan Heights (the ‘Alpha line’). Do not attempt to enter the occupied Golan Heights through Syria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sheba’a Farms and Ghajja"]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["The rest of the West Bank, except for: East Jerusalem, Bethlehem Governate, Ramallah Municipality, Jericho municipality and all areas which lie south of it (this includes the Allenby crossing). Highway 1 that links Jerusalem and Tel Aviv and the areas that lie to the south and west of the Highway (this includes Highway 3), and Route 443 and Highway 45 which link Jerusalem and Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and military infrastructure. There remains a risk of further attacks across the region at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palestine/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Shelter in place"]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow the instructions of the local authorities. If you are advised to take shelter, ",["Israel’s Home Front Command provides guidance on how to find a protected space","https://www.oref.org.il/eng/emergencies/protection-guidelines"],". The best option is a residential protected space (Mamad, Mamak or Maman) or a communal shelter. If that is not possible, choose a stairwell without windows and exterior walls and stay at its centre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to receive information and alerts. Visit ",["Israel’s Home Front Command","https://www.oref.org.il/eng"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["If you are in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to ongoing regional tensions, we recommend against all travel to some parts of Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation could escalate quickly and poses significant risks. Regional tensions may cause international borders (air and land) to close."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Israel and Palestine, be aware that whilst the frequency of missile and drone attacks has decreased there is a risk of rocket and drone attacks throughout Israel. There is a risk of shrapnel from intercepted missiles falling across Israel and Palestine, and possible disruption at Ben Gurion airport in Tel Aviv."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political tension can cause demonstrations and clashes around anniversaries and significant events."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date through local media and follow the instructions of Israeli Home Front Command. To find these:"]},{"k":"li","s":["visit the Israeli Home Front Command website (available in Israel only)"]},{"k":"li","s":["call 104 if you are in Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling within Israel or Palestine, check the local measures in place, that roads are open and, where appropriate, that scheduled train and bus services are operating."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel within or out of Israel or Palestine is at your own risk. You are encouraged to follow the advice of local authorities, for example on which routes are open or when to take shelter."]},{"k":"h","s":["Leaving Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["Border crossings out of Gaza have been closed to civilians and general traffic since the Israeli military took control of the Rafah crossing on 6 May 2024. Consular support is not available from within Gaza. If you are a British national in Gaza who wants to leave Gaza, you should make contact with us as soon as possible. There are currently no exit routes available for foreign nationals to depart Gaza independently. We are working with the Israeli, Palestinian and other authorities in the region to help British nationals leave via safe routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a UK visa holder who meets all of the following criteria, you can contact us to request support to leave Gaza if:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have a spouse/partner or a child aged 17 or under currently living in the UK, and"]},{"k":"li","s":["you hold valid permission to enter or remain in the UK for longer than 6 months"]},{"k":"h","s":["Help from other organisations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date with local travel advice through local news outlets and international outlets like the Access Coordination Unit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide and any specific travel advice that applies to you:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["disabled travellers","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["volunteering and adventure travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help British nationals make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel despite FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Israel and Palestine set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Israeli Embassy in London","https://embassies.gov.il/london/Pages/default.aspx"]," or the ",["Palestinian Mission to the UK","https://palmissionuk.org/consular-affairs-ar/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check Israeli immigration policies before you travel. Allow extra time for increased security measures and checks at airports, especially during Israeli holidays and during the summer tourist season."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Israel or Palestine, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 90 days after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Israel without a visa as a tourist. On entry, visitors get permission to stay for up to 3 months. However, if you are a dual national, read the ",["dual nationals guidance","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/entry-requirements#british-people-holding-dual-nationality"]," for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you work in Israel without the proper permissions, you can be detained and deported. This process could take several months."]},{"k":"h","s":["Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA)"]},{"k":"p","s":["As of 1 January 2025, to visit Israel you will need to get an Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) before you arrive. The ETA is valid for 2 years and covers a visit of 90 days. It will cost 25 new Israeli shekels. You can check your eligibility and ",["apply for an ETA with the Israel Population and Immigration authority","https://israel-entry.piba.gov.il/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Passport stamping and entry cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Visitors entering via Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport get an entry card instead of an entry stamp in their passport. At other entry points to the country, you may get an entry card or you may get a stamp."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your entry card with your passport until you leave. This is evidence that you entered Israel legally. You may need it, particularly if you’re crossing into Palestine. If you’re refused entry to Israel, your passport may be stamped with an entry stamp and 2 red lines drawn across it to show the refusal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Stamps with restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Entry stamps that state ‘Palestinian Authority only’ or ‘Judea and Samaria only’ have been issued to some travellers at:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Allenby Bridge crossing with Jordan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since travellers entering by the Allenby Bridge crossing must pass through Israeli checkpoints and Israeli-controlled territory to reach Jerusalem or Gaza, this effectively limits travellers who receive this stamp."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not clear how travellers who get this stamp at Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport can leave the airport without violating the restriction."]},{"k":"p","s":["This stamp has been issued to travellers who have no Palestinian or other Arab ancestry, and do not seem to have a claim to a Palestinian Authority ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Immigration checks"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Israeli authorities decide if you can enter Israel. You may experience lengthy personal questioning and baggage searches at security when you enter and leave Israel. Some visitors may face longer searches and questioning, including those:"]},{"k":"li","s":["with Palestinian or Arab ancestry, or with ancestry of a country that is predominantly Muslim"]},{"k":"li","s":["with evidence of previous travel which may be considered suspicious"]},{"k":"li","s":["who are considered to have publicly criticised the state of Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals can legally be refused entry if they:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have publicly called for a boycott of Israel or Israeli settlements"]},{"k":"li","s":["belong to an organisation which has called for a boycott"]},{"k":"li","s":["have publicly made statements denying the Holocaust or the October 7 terrorist attack"]},{"k":"li","s":["have publicly made statements of support for the prosecution of Israeli citizens in a foreign country or in an international court for actions they took during their military duties for Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers, particularly those who fall into these categories, may be held at border control for more checks, sometimes for several hours, including in detention facilities. Israeli security has sometimes requested access to travellers’ personal email or social media accounts as a condition of entry. Your baggage or digital devices may also be searched and could be withheld."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Previous travel to countries in the region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Evidence of previous travel to another country in the region, such as entry or exit stamps in your passport, does not normally stop you entering Israel. However, you may face extra questioning at the border."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have concerns about visas or entry into Israel, including whether previous travel can affect you travelling there, contact the Israeli Embassy in the UK before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refusal of entry into Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re refused entry to Israel, you will be booked on the next available flight back to where you flew in from, on the same airline."]},{"k":"p","s":["Depending on the flight schedule, you may be taken to the Immigration Detention Centre (a few minutes’ drive from the airport) to wait until your flight departs. You will have access to a telephone, information in English and medical assistance if needed. Your luggage will stay at the airport, so tell officials if you need to retrieve anything urgent from your luggage, for example medication."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can contact the ",["British Embassy in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-tel-aviv"]," from the detention centre. They can help where possible but cannot intervene in immigration decisions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entering Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Israeli authorities control entry to Palestine, including by sea to Gaza. You must show a passport and Israeli immigration slip to cross between Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about the ",["requirements for foreign nationals entering the West Bank on the Israeli government website","https://www.gov.il/en/departments/policies/judeaentry2022"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Israeli border officials at Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport have asked some travellers to sign a form stating they are not allowed to enter territories controlled by the Palestinian Authority unless they get advance authorisation from the Israeli ‘Territory Actions Co-ordinator’. You can be deported from Israel and barred from entry for up to 10 years for violating this restriction."]},{"k":"p","s":["If immigration officials believe you plan to enter Gaza without permission, or that you’re entering Israel to work in Palestine, they may refuse you entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot support your application for entry or exit permits for Gaza. If you decide to visit Gaza against FCDO advice, you must contact the relevant authorities well in advance. FCDO cannot provide administrative support to UK charities wishing to enter Gaza by the Rafah crossing."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Rafah border regularly closes with no warning and for long periods. The Erez border is currently closed. At these times it may be impossible to enter or leave Gaza."]},{"k":"p","s":["Israeli checkpoints may close on Israeli public holidays and during periods of increased instability. There have been increased movement and access restrictions across the West Bank with unpredictable opening and closing times. There is information on ",["known checkpoint closures on the UN website","https://www.accesscoordination.org/"],". This can change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals may encounter suspicion or hostility at checkpoints and in areas not frequented by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["British nationals of Palestinian origin"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national of Palestinian origin (on the Palestinian Population Register or holding a Palestinian ID number), you must have a Palestinian passport or travel document to leave Gaza or the West Bank."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national with a Palestinian name or place of birth but without a Palestinian ID number, you may face problems. British nationals of Palestinian origin or British nationals married to Palestinians have been refused entry into Israel."]},{"k":"h","s":["British people holding dual nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["British-Palestinian dual nationals living in the West Bank and Gaza may only exit Palestine through the Allenby border crossing into Jordan or the Rafah border crossing into Egypt. They must return by the same route."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British-Palestinian dual national entering Gaza against FCDO travel advice, check entry and exit procedures with the relevant authorities. There is a limit on the number of dual nationals permitted to enter and exit Gaza through Erez – this includes if you are entering for medical or humanitarian reasons. The Israeli government has the authority to make decisions on entry and exit permits through Erez."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your nearest Israeli embassy if you need pre-approval to travel to Israel. Dual nationals holding Iranian, Iraqi, Syrian and Lebanese citizenship have previously been affected. If you are not a citizen of any of these countries, but have close family ties, you should check with your nearest Israeli embassy before travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Children with at least one Israeli parent (father or mother) are considered Israeli nationals. These children must enter and leave Israel on an Israeli passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["British nationals with associations with other countries in the region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dual nationals holding Iranian, Iraqi, Syrian and Lebanese citizenship have previously been heavily questioned, denied entry and deported. If a deportation flight is not available immediately, this can mean being detained until one is available, which can take a number of days. If you are a citizen of any of these countries, or have associations such as close family ties, the Israeli authorities advise you to check with your nearest Israeli embassy before travel to get pre-approval for entry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Children and young people"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 17 and under travelling to Israel alone or with only one parent should carry a letter from their parents or guardians confirming parental consent, accommodation plans and contact details."]},{"k":"p","s":["Children exiting Israel alone should carry a locally-issued notarised letter as advised by ",["external law firms","https://lawoffice.org.il/en/unaccompanied-minors-traveling-abroad-from-israel/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For children with at least one Israeli parent, read the advice for dual nationals above."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry to Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["Egypt-Israel border crossing (opening times are subject to change):"]},{"k":"li","s":["Taba: Open 24 hours"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to cross the border from Israel into Egypt at Taba, we recommend you bring at least 170 US dollars (cash) per person, with some extra US dollars in cash to cover any further expenses. Since early March 2026, border crossing charges at Taba have been subject to increases at short notice."]},{"k":"li","s":["If staying in Taba, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 20 US dollars. The border tax allows you to obtain an entry permission stamp for a stay of up to 15 days"]},{"k":"li","s":["If travelling further than Taba, including to Sharm El-Sheikh, but remaining within the Sinai Peninsula, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 120 US dollars. The border tax allows you to obtain an entry permission stamp for a stay of up to 15 days"]},{"k":"li","s":["If travelling beyond the Sinai Peninsula, including to fly from airports such as Cairo and Hurghada, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 120 US dollars and purchase a standard entry visa for 30 US dollars. At Taba, this entry visa also requires a “letter of guarantee”, provided by travel agents and costing around 20 USD. Both the visa and the “letter of guarantee” can be purchased at the Border Crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["If travelling by car through the Taba Border Crossing you may also be required to pay 100 US dollars and additional amounts for parking."]},{"k":"p","s":["Please note that ATMs at the Taba Border Crossing are unreliable and frequently run out of cash. Travellers should obtain USD before travelling or in Eilat before arriving at the Crossing as all payments are required in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials may ask travellers to remove hats, coats or other items of clothing, including religious clothing, as they pass through the Taba Border Crossing terminal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry to Jordan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Land crossings to Jordan may be restricted or close at short notice, including due to trade union strikes. More information is available on the ",["Israel Airport Authority website","https://www.iaa.gov.il/en/land-border-crossings/alenbi/notifications-and-updates/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jordan-Israel border crossings (opening times are subject to change):"]},{"k":"li","s":["Allenby/King Hussein Bridge"]},{"k":"li","s":["The Northern (Jordan River/Sheikh Hussein) crossing"]},{"k":"li","s":["The Southern (Yitzhak Rabin/Wadi Araba) crossing"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip, check the vaccinations and certificates you need in ",["TravelHealthPro’s Israel guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/110/israel#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," and ",["TravelHealthPro’s Palestinian guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/173/palestinian#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Israel and Palestine","https://www.gov.il/en/departments/topics/customs_israel_tax_authority/govil-landing-page"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Israeli Tax Authority provides information on ",["taking money into or out of Israel","https://www.gov.il/en/departments/guides/guide-requirement-report-and-spend-money-on-israel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict between Lebanese Hizballah and Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and Lebanese Hizballah (LH), a cessation of hostilities was announced on 16 April 2026. However, fighting continues and the dynamic nature of the conflict means the situation may change quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict between Iran and Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and Iran a ceasefire was agreed on 8 April 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict between the Houthis (in Yemen) and Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and the Houthis (in Yemen), there continues to be a risk of missile and drone attacks throughout Israel. There is a risk of shrapnel from intercepted missiles falling across Israel and Palestine and possible disruption at Ben Gurion airport. On 22 and 24 September 2025, two drones fired by the Houthis fell in Eilat, injuring at least 20 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 7 October 2023 there was a large-scale terrorist attack by Hamas in southern Israel. The frequency of attacks has significantly decreased but there is still a risk of rocket attacks throughout Israel."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increased risk of political tension which can cause demonstrations and clashes around anniversaries and significant events."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["There was a large-scale terrorist attack by Hamas into southern Israel on 7 October 2023 where over 1,200 people were killed. Hamas continue to launch rockets into Israel and the Israeli Defence Forces are conducting significant military activity in Gaza."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Israel and Palestine are very likely to continue with an increased threat of attacks, including by individuals acting alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any attacks could be indiscriminate, including places visited by foreign nationals such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Old City in Jerusalem"]},{"k":"li","s":["government, military and police installations"]},{"k":"li","s":["security personnel including military and police"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport networks"]},{"k":"li","s":["businesses with western interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places"]},{"k":"p","s":["Areas where foreign nationals and tourists are known to gather may be at higher risk of attack. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of recent significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2025:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in September, six people were killed and eight wounded in a shooting attack in northern Jerusalem"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March, one person was killed and one person injured in a shooting attack in northern Israel"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March, one person was killed and 3 injured in a stabbing attack in Haifa"]},{"k":"li","s":["in February, one person was killed and 12 people were injured in a ramming and stabbing attack at Karkur Junction near Pardes Hana-Karkur, south of Haifa"]},{"k":"li","s":["in February, 3 bombs exploded on 3 separate busses in the Tel Aviv area. Two other buses were found with bombs which failed to explode. There were no casualties. See our Regional Risks section for further information on using public transport in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024:"]},{"k":"li","s":["7 people were killed in a shooting and stabbing attack in Jaffa"]},{"k":"li","s":["3 people were killed in a shooting attack at the Allenby Bridge Crossing"]},{"k":"li","s":["one person was killed and 17 injured during a ramming attack in Ra’anana"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2023:"]},{"k":"li","s":["3 people were killed during a shooting attack in the Jordan Valley"]},{"k":"li","s":["one person was killed and 6 people injured during a car-ramming incident in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"li","s":["one person was killed and 3 people injured in a shooting attack in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"li","s":["7 people were killed and 3 injured during a shooting attack in Neve Yaakov, East Jerusalem"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist kidnap is a risk in Gaza and along the border with Egypt. On 7 October 2023, 251 people were kidnapped by Hamas into Gaza."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is to not make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was an ongoing conflict between Israel and Hamas following the October 7 2023 Hamas terrorist attack which saw 251 people kidnapped into Gaza. On 10 October, Hamas and Israel agreed to a ceasefire."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. You should check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice. If travelling near military operation areas, follow all Israeli official instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Military activity continues on the Gaza border. Keep up to date with the news while travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date with local travel advice on local news outlets and international outlets like the Access Coordination Unit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rocket fire can affect most areas of Israel and the interception of missiles over Palestine may result in falling fragments or debris. Israeli air strikes also continue into Gaza. Be cautious and make sure you know the safety actions that you should take if an Israeli warning siren sounds. Follow ",["advice from local authorities","https://www.idf.il/en/minisites/regional-commands/home-front-command/how-to-act-during-an-alert/"]," and stay informed of the security situation through the media and this travel advice. No warning sirens will sound inside Gaza, or in the West Bank outside of Israeli settlements. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/regional-risks#gaza"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Violent incidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Israel and the West Bank, there is a risk of violent incidents, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stabbings"]},{"k":"li","s":["shootings"]},{"k":"li","s":["arson"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicle rammings"]},{"k":"li","s":["stone throwing attacks on people and vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["explosions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents have occurred:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Be’er Sheva"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Hadera"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Jerusalem and the Old City, particularly at and around: Damascus Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Herod’s gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lion’s Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chain Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Nablus"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Jenin"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Hebron"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Jordan Valley"]},{"k":"li","s":["along Route 60 (especially junctions near Nablus), Route 443 and other West Bank arterial roads used by both Palestinians and Israelis"]},{"k":"li","s":["at Israeli checkpoints"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents have involved protestors (Israelis and Palestinians), Israeli security forces and civilians, including Israeli settlers. Tourists or bystanders could be caught up in incidents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Demonstrations and armed clashes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Large political demonstrations can:"]},{"k":"li","s":["happen across Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"li","s":["happen at short notice and often turn violent"]},{"k":"li","s":["affect entry and exit to Ben Gurion Airport in Tel Aviv-check before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check local news before travelling for information on recent clashes"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large gatherings and demonstrations"]},{"k":"li","s":["check locally before travelling to areas where there has been recent violence and follow the instructions of the local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If Israeli security operations or armed clashes are happening near you, stay inside and wait for the local authorities to confirm that the situation is calm before moving to a different location."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is increased risk of political tension, which can cause demonstrations and clashes, during events such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Thursday and Saturday evenings"]},{"k":"li","s":["after Friday prayers"]},{"k":"li","s":["Jewish high holidays (Passover, Rosh Hashana, Yom Kippur and Succoth)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ramadan, in particular Laylat Al Qadr"]},{"k":"li","s":["other religious holidays"]},{"k":"li","s":["anniversaries including 7 October, Independence Day (14 May, Hebrew calendar dates vary), Jerusalem Day (date varies), Land Day (30 March), Nakba Day (15 May)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Risks increase when religious or national holidays overlap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some of these protests have led to violent clashes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refugee camps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be extremely cautious if visiting refugee camps. Hebron and Palestinian refugee camps have previously been the site of violent clashes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Settlements"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been recent violent incidents in settlements and settlement outposts, including near Beit El, Homesh, Shilo and Evyatar."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your personal belongings in a safe place. Theft of passports, credit cards, and valuables from public beaches is common."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry ID, for example, a copy of the personal details and entry stamp pages of your passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Jerusalem, the West Bank and Gaza, clothing should cover your shoulders, upper arms, and legs above the knee."]},{"k":"p","s":["Locals in ultra-Orthodox Jewish neighbourhoods such as Bnei Brak, Modi’in Illit, Beitar Illit, Beit Shemesh and Safed can react strongly to anyone, particularly women, dressed less conservatively. Check locations of ultra-Orthodox neighbourhoods and towns in travel guides."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. If you are in Palestine during this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 7 and under do not fast during Ramadan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access and prayers at Al-Aqsa Mosque during Ramadan have seen restrictions and heightened security measures by Israeli authorities. This includes age and gender-based entry restrictions, and routine physical searches. There will be a heightened security environment and tense atmosphere during Ramadan in the Old City."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk or be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying property"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are risks in buying property in Israeli settlements on land considered to be occupied under international law in East Jerusalem, the rest of the West Bank and the Golan. A future peace deal between Israel and the Palestinians, or between Israel and Syria, could have consequences for property you buy in these settlements."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO does not offer legal advice on or become involved in private property disputes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught with drugs, you can expect a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be sensitive about taking pictures of people in Muslim and Orthodox Jewish areas. Do not take photographs of military or police officers or installations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Israeli law does not criminalise same-sex sexual relations between consenting adults. In Palestine, same-sex sexual activity is legal in the West Bank but illegal in Gaza, where it carries a 10-year prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attitudes towards LGBT+ issues in some parts of Palestinian and Israeli society can be hostile."]},{"k":"p","s":["In more conservative Israeli areas in the West Bank, including in ultra-Orthodox communities, if you show affection in public, regardless of your gender or sexuality, you may receive negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Palestinian society, same-sex relationships are largely taboo. Some Palestinian groups may violently oppose cultural events and demonstrations, which they see as inconsistent with their values. This includes those seen as linked to the LGBT+ community, even if the event is not intended to promote LGBT+ rights. In these cases, the Palestinian security forces and police may not always act effectively to protect participants. Be aware of these risks. Liaise with local authorities before planning or organising any event."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tel Aviv has a large, active LGBT+ community and a big annual Pride parade. Jerusalem also has an annual Pride parade, but there has been a heavy security presence at the event since a fatal stabbing in 2015. Be aware of your personal security if attending."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught breaking local laws on import and export of wild animals, expect to receive a substantial fine and up to 2 years in prison. For more information on the regulations and laws in Israel see the ",["Israeli Nature and Park Authority website","https://en.parks.org.il/%D7%99%D7%91%D7%95%D7%90-%D7%95%D7%99%D7%A6%D7%95%D7%90-%D7%97%D7%99%D7%95%D7%AA-%D7%91%D7%A8-%D7%95%D7%A2%D7%A8%D7%9B%D7%99-%D7%98%D7%91%D7%A2-%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%92%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%9D/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Israel and Palestine, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["carry a green card","https://www.gov.uk/vehicle-insurance/driving-abroad"]," to prove you have the minimum insurance cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent road accidents, due to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["erratic driving"]},{"k":"li","s":["unreliable vehicle maintenance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police operate radar speed traps on some roads and issue heavy fines for speeding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid driving into ultra-Orthodox Jewish areas of Jerusalem on Shabbat. Shabbat is from sunset on Friday to nightfall on Saturday. If you attempt to drive into these areas, local residents may throw stones at your car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiring a car"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to drive across into the West Bank, check your insurance will cover you there. Some hire companies do not insure vehicles taken there. It may be easier to hire a fully insured car from a company in East Jerusalem."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hitchhiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not safe to hitchhike in Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving in the desert"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to the desert, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["go with others"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a supply of water"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a mobile phone"]},{"k":"li","s":["let someone know your itinerary and expected return time"]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads can flood during extreme weather conditions. Flash flooding is a risk, particularly in the arid southern region of the Negev. Check risk areas locally."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Israel and Palestine. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Israel and Palestine. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Jerusalem"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 7 October Israeli authorities have limited access to Jerusalem, and Israel in general, for residents of the West Bank, enforcing age and gender-specific restrictions for entry, particularly during Ramadan. While women aged 51 or over and men aged 56 or over with special permits have been granted entry for prayers, many potential worshippers have been turned away. Additionally, there have been routine instances of physical searches and detentions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Street protests and demonstrations can happen across Jerusalem, including East Jerusalem and the Old City. Check local news ahead of travel and follow instructions of local authorities. Avoid demonstrations and large gatherings."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent demonstrations in many of the areas visited by tourists in the Old City and after Friday prayers. Areas include in and around:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Damascus Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Herod’s Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lion’s Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Chain Gate"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some protests have led to violent clashes. Be aware of your surroundings at all times and leave the area if there is evidence of tension or unrest, for example if the shops in the souks of the Old City suddenly begin to close their shutters. The entrances to the Old City may have additional checks, or may close."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been a number of violent incidents on public transport and near public transport lines. Take extra care when using public transport in Jerusalem."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care when using public transport in Tel Aviv, in particular at transport hubs, and when using buses in the greater Tel Aviv area. Consider using other forms of transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been large political demonstrations in Tel Aviv. Entry and exit to Ben Gurion airport has occasionally been impacted during demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas near Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been repeated instances of rocket fire from Gaza, which may reach well beyond the Gaza border area. Israel has often responded with air strikes into Gaza. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you know the safety actions to take if an Israeli warning siren sounds – no warning sirens will sound inside Gaza"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow ",["advice from local authorities","https://www.idf.il/en/minisites/regional-commands/home-front-command/how-to-act-during-an-alert/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["stay informed of the security situation through the media"]},{"k":"h","s":["Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Gaza (including the waters off Gaza)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not approach the perimeter fence surrounding the Gaza Strip."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot offer routine consular assistance in Gaza. If you travel to Gaza against our advice, review your security arrangements regularly."]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossings with Israel (Erez) and Egypt (Rafah) may close with no notice. Check the status of the Rafah crossing into Egypt before you travel. Movement to the Rafah crossing and beyond is at your own risk. Currently, the Rafah border regularly closes with no warning and for long periods. The Erez border has been closed since October 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["There will be no warning siren inside Gaza and there are no official air raid shelters. Take advice from locals about the safest place to shelter."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot help individuals applying for entry or exit permits for Gaza. See ",["entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO recognises that major international organisations need to carry out humanitarian and reconstruction work and engage in independent reporting and verification of the situation in Gaza. Medical and other essential specialist staff should co-ordinate their entry to and exit from Gaza with those organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not enter Gaza by sea, including via a flotilla delivering humanitarian aid. The Israeli Navy routinely patrols the area and will prevent any vessels attempting to breach the restrictions – see ",["entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/entry-requirements"],". You will be detained and deported, and your electronic equipment is likely to be confiscated. FCDO does not believe that humanitarian supplies should be delivered in this way. If you send humanitarian assistance or other goods to Gaza, use established channels."]},{"k":"h","s":["Israel-Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was an ongoing conflict between Israel and Lebanese Hizballah (LH). On 27 November 2024, LH and Israel agreed to a ceasefire, with a 60-day implementation period. Hostilities resumed in 2026 with a ceasefire agreed on 16 April."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. You should check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice. If travelling near military operation areas, follow all Israeli official instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Military activity continues on the Israel-Lebanon border. Keep up to date with the news while travelling. See also section on Conflict with Lebanese Hizballah."]},{"k":"h","s":["Israel-Syria border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 500m of the border with Syria (the ‘Alpha Line’)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation is fragile, with military exchanges either side of the border. If you’re travelling in the area, be aware of your personal security, check local media and follow advice from local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Occupied Golan Heights"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 500m of the Area of Separation in the occupied Golan Heights (the ‘Alpha line’). Do not attempt to enter the occupied Golan Heights through Syria."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Sheba’a Farms and Ghajjar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and Lebanese Hizballah, a ceasefire was agreed on 27 November. There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. In the occupied Golan Heights, restrictions may be put in place at short notice. Rocket attacks and sporadic gunfire occur without warning. There is also a risk of falling debris from Israeli and Syrian air defence systems."]},{"k":"p","s":["Landmines have been planted across the occupied Golan Heights, including near to populated areas and roads. These areas are usually marked and often fenced off. Follow established roads and paths. FCDO long-standing advice has been to not hike off-trail. If you’re in the region, follow advice from local law enforcement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border with Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation on the border with Egypt is volatile. Take extra care when using the Route 10 road, which runs along the Israeli border with Egypt. Route 10 is sometimes closed by the Israeli authorities. Consider using other routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent clashes between Israeli Security Forces and Palestinians in these areas and violent incidents can occur without warning."]},{"k":"h","s":["West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been a heightened state of tension and violent clashes resulting in deaths in the West Bank since the outbreak of conflict in October 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["Expect road closures and numerous checkpoints across the West Bank."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no warning sirens or official air raid shelters inside the West Bank, outside of Israeli settlements."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot travel into or out of the West Bank without passing through at least one Israeli military checkpoint. You need a passport and immigration slip to go through these checkpoints. Checkpoints may be closed during Jewish high holidays, Israeli public holidays and periods of increased instability restricting movement in and out of the West Bank. This does not normally affect foreign nationals, but would affect British-Palestinian dual nationals. Road closures can occur with little notice. Keep up to date with local travel advice through local media, and international information outlets like the UN’s Access Coordination Unit."]},{"k":"p","s":["The cities of Bethlehem, Ramallah and Jericho see large numbers of tourists including on organised tours, although tourist numbers have reduced since 7 October 2023. While there have been no recent reports of any serious incidents involving foreigners, you should take care when travelling anywhere in the West Bank."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent incidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violent incidents and demonstrations in the West Bank (see ",["Political situation","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/safety-and-security"]," for details). If you are in a location where an Israeli security operation or armed clashes are ongoing, stay inside and wait for the local authorities to confirm that the situation is calm before moving to a different location."]},{"k":"p","s":["Israelis living in the illegal settlements in the West Bank occasionally organise demonstrations which can turn violent. There are reports that settlers have threatened people travelling near to settlements and settlement outposts. Take care if you are near settlements, including those in the hills around Nablus, in the South Hebron hills and settlement outposts."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a closed military zone in the H2 area of Hebron (around Ash-Shuhada Street and the Ibrahimi Mosque/Tomb of the Patriarchs), where there is a risk of a hostile reaction from members of extremist groups."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be particularly cautious if considering a visit to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Hebron or Palestinian refugee camps which have previously been the site of violent clashes – FCDO advises against all travel to the camps in Jenin and Nablus"]},{"k":"li","s":["settlements and settlement outposts where there have been recent violent incidents – for example, near Beit El, Homesh, Shilo, Evyatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid these locations after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents have also occurred along Route 60 (especially junctions near Nablus), Route 443 and other West Bank arterial roads used by both Palestinians and Israelis. Use extreme caution on these routes, particularly at night, and leave if you see any signs of a disturbance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transport in the West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["We advise you not to use taxis in the West Bank, because of their involvement in a significant number of accidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid using buses in the West Bank and consider the difficulties and risks of travelling between Jerusalem and Ramallah via checkpoints, along Route 60 (especially the junctions near Nablus), Route 443 and other West Bank arterial roads used by both Palestinians and Israelis."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["For an ambulance dial:"]},{"k":"li","s":["100 in Israel"]},{"k":"li","s":["101 in the West Bank and Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Israel","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/110/israel#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," and ",["Palestine","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/173/palestinian#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Israel","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/110/israel#General_Information"]," and ",["Palestine","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/173/palestinian"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare in Israel and Palestine is not free and medical treatment can be expensive. Hospitals will insist on payment and may take legal action to stop you leaving until bills are paid. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has lists of ",["medical providers in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-list-of-medical-facilities"]," and ",["medical providers in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Israel and Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/information-for-british-nationals-residing-in-israel-and-the-opts#healthcare-in-israel-and-the-opts"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 101"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 102"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 100"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["English-speaking lawyers in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-list-of-lawyers"]," and ",["English-speaking lawyers in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-list-of-lawyers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["translators and interpreters in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-list-of-translators"]," and ",["translators and interpreters in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-list-of-lawyers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Israel and Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-israel-the-opts"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-prisoner-pack"]," and ",["arrested or imprisoned in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/the-occupied-palestinian-territories/british-consulate-general-jerusalem"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/the-occupied-palestinian-territories/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers information and advice for ",["British companies operating overseas in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-israel"]," and ",["British companies operating overseas in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-palestinian-territories"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":47613,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/what-happens-after-a-midterm-tsunami-lessons-from-1974-and-1994-296034":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"f53af87c1751008c1f665384f7f650d76c6f58690366fd7337e45c7e4cb6eea9","read":"https://theconversation.com/what-happens-after-a-midterm-tsunami-lessons-from-1974-and-1994-296034","bytes":184173,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What happens after a midterm tsunami? Lessons from 1974 and 1994","by":[{"n":"Robert A. Strong","r":"Senior Fellow, Miller Center, University of Virginia"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T19:56:16Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["There were lots of surprises on the evening of Nov. 3 when the picture of the Democratic midterm success began to be painted on network news touch screens."]},{"k":"p","s":["The maps kept getting bluer. Eventually, it was clear that this was not an ordinary midterm cycle when the party out of power slaps the wrist of the sitting president and his administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was much bigger than that, something on a scale the U.S. has seen only two times in the past half-century."]},{"k":"p","s":["One was the ",["Newt Gingrich “revolution”","https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/november-8/the-republican-revolution"]," in 1994 that put Republicans in control of the House of Representatives for the first time in 40 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["The other was the election of 1974 that flooded Capitol Hill with “Watergate babies” – new members elected just after the Nixon-era scandals."]},{"k":"p","s":["In both cases there were high hopes that big changes would take place in the aftermath of remarkable midterm elections. The actual results were more modest than the victors expected."]},{"k":"h","s":["1994’s wipeout election"]},{"k":"p","s":["The 1994 midterm elections gave the Republican Party a dramatic victory. The Democrats lost their majority in the Senate, and 54 seats were flipped in the House of Representatives, making ",["Gingrich","https://history.house.gov/People/Detail/13850"]," the first Republican speaker of the House since Eisenhower lived in the White House."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was a wipeout election that had not been expected, and it changed the dynamics of Democrat ",["Bill Clinton’s presidency","https://millercenter.org/president/clinton/impact-and-legacy"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The combative Gingrich","https://www.npr.org/2018/11/01/662906525/combative-tribal-angry-newt-gingrich-set-the-stage-for-trump-journalist-says"]," emerged as a political celebrity; partisanship intensified and gridlock became the new norm. Confrontations over spending led to controversial ",["government shutdowns","https://millercenter.org/1995-96-government-shutdown"]," and the first modern threat to ",["default on America’s debt obligations","https://www.npr.org/2019/01/12/683304824/the-longest-government-shutdown-in-history-no-longer-how-1995-changed-everything"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Because the new Republican congressional majorities appeared to overreach in their efforts to cut taxes and spending, ",["Clinton was able to recover sufficient popularity","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/governing-in-an-age-of-no-majorities-bill-clintons-mission-for-a-second-term/"]," to win a second term."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the run-up to his bid for reelection, ",["Clinton took the electoral rebuke of 1994 to heart","https://www.politico.com/story/2007/01/clintons-state-of-union-helped-turn-around-loss-of-congress-002416"]," and followed a centrist strategy that represented a move to the right of longtime Democratic positions on welfare, crime and immigration. He continued to oppose many Republican policy proposals but worked with Republicans to craft ",["welfare reform legislation","https://cosm.aei.org/lessons-from-the-1996-welfare-reform-law-approaching-its-30th-anniversary/"]," and new bills dealing with ",["crime","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-signing-the-violent-crime-control-and-law-enforcement-act-1994"]," and ",["immigration","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/the-presidents-radio-address-317"],". Budget confrontation eventually gave way to compromise, and for a few years in the late 1990s ",["the United States had a balanced budget","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/how-did-the-budget-get-balanced-in-the-late-1990s/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Partisanship became more personal in Clinton’s second term when ",["Gingrich pushed for impeachment","https://millercenter.org/the-presidency/impeachment/clinton-impeachment-and-its-fallout"]," following the revelations of the president’s affair with Monica Lewinsky."]},{"k":"p","s":["Clinton, with a tarnished reputation, ",["survived his Senate trial","https://www.theguardian.com/world/1999/feb/12/clinton.usa2"],". Ironically, it was ",["Gingrich who resigned","https://www.nytimes.com/1998/11/07/us/the-speaker-steps-down-the-career-the-fall-of-gingrich-an-irony-in-an-odd-year.html"]," after failing to remove the president at the ballot box or in the impeachment process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gingrich, the biggest winner in the 1994 midterms, left office with a promised revolution largely unrealized."]},{"k":"h","s":["1974’s Watergate reformers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Going back even further in American political history, the midterm elections following President ",["Richard Nixon’s resignation after the Watergate scandal","https://www.gilderlehrman.org/sites/default/files/2024-12/GLI_Resignation%20Speech%20Nixon_2024_printer.pdf"]," produced a Democratic Party victory."]},{"k":"p","s":["That victory was not a surprise; the scale of it was."]},{"k":"p","s":["Democrats, who already had majorities in the House and Senate, ",["won a huge margin in the congressional popular vote","https://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2014/11/the-democrats-high-water-mark-came-40-years-ago-112492"]," and brought new members to both chambers ",["who were younger, more liberal","https://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2018/05/26/congress-broke-american-politics-218544/"]," and ",["reform-minded","https://www.nytimes.com/2019/01/03/opinion/house-democrats-watergate-1974.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["They wanted to prevent future Watergates. New laws would make the ",["government more open, more honest and more accountable","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/watergate-babies-midterms/"],". New and more staff would allow Congress to be less reliant on executive branch information and better able to act in foreign policy and budget management. Special prosecutors would be appointed to investigate abuses of power and violations of law."]},{"k":"p","s":["A Democrat, Jimmy Carter, ",["would be elected president","https://www.270towin.com/1976-election/"]," two years after the massive 1974 midterm victory, and more reform legislation would be passed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["post-Watergate congressional agenda was long and bold","https://www.aei.org/events/watergate-revisited-the-reforms-and-the-reality-40-years-later/"]," – the war powers resolution, a freedom of information act, the creation of inspectors general, campaign finance reform, a presidential records act and new legislation to regulate foreign intelligence surveillance and the bribing of foreign officials."]},{"k":"p","s":["These new laws were supposed to stop, or uncover, the kind of wrongdoing that made Nixon an ",["imperial president","https://www.govexec.com/federal-news/2006/02/imperial-presidency-has-long-history/21214/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new laws and institutions certainly made a difference – ",["but not without creating their own problems","https://hls.harvard.edu/today/watergate-era-reforms-50-years-later/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["All the post-Watergate presidents thought ",["the war powers resolution was unconstitutional","https://dornsife.usc.edu/scribe/2026/09/18/is-the-war-powers-resolution-constitutional/"],", objecting to its restrictions on the president’s authority as commander in chief, and ",["U.S. military interventions overseas continued to occur","https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R42738"],". Special prosecutors ",["conducted many investigations","https://www.washingtonpost.com/history/2019/03/19/whiskey-watergate-whitewater-how-special-prosecutor-robert-muellers-predecessors-made-history/"],", but often at great expense and without adequate supervision or meaningful results."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carter, narrowly elected president in 1976, served only one term and ",["lost reelection to Ronald Reagan","https://www.270towin.com/1980-election/"],", who fully restored the Republican Party’s dominance in presidential politics."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over time, many presidents, ",["especially Donald Trump","https://www.opb.org/article/2025/02/15/trumps-efforts-with-doge-cuts-test-watergate-era-reforms/"],", dismantled or ignored important elements of the post-Watergate reforms."]},{"k":"p","s":["The large and enthusiastic congressional majorities that took power after the 1974 midterms were energetic but produced ",["a political legacy with complicated and controversial results","https://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2018/05/26/congress-broke-american-politics-218544/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Chaos and conflict – or compromise?"]},{"k":"p","s":["What is the country likely to see in the next few months and the next two years?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Will it be chaos, conflict and occasional compromise, like the politics that followed the midterms in 1994? Or will it be earnest and sometimes heavy-handed congressional efforts to investigate and prevent presidential wrongdoing, like those that swept through Washington after 1974?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Surprising midterm elections that create new majorities on Capitol Hill look to be revolutions in the days after they occur. Years later, they often appear to be more complex – and less significant."]}],"chars":5752}};
